$DATUM Ethyl 2-(2-Fluoro-4-iodoanilino)acetate (41h). To a solution of 40 (100
mg, 0.4 mmol) in EtOH (10 mL) at 0 °C were added c-HCl (0.1 mL) and ethyl
glyoxylate (0.17 mL, 0.8 mmol). The reaction mixture was stirred for 30
min at ambient temperature, and sodium cyanoborohydride (55.6 mg, 0.8
mmol) was added. The resulting reaction mixture was extracted with EtOAc,
and the combined organic layers were washed with brine, dried over MgSO4,
and concentrated in vacuo. Purification of the residue by flash column
chromatography (EtOAc:n-hexane ) 1:10) afforded 133 mg (98%) of 41h:
Ethyl 2-(2-Fluoro-4-iodoanilino)acetate (41h), yield 133 mg (98%) 1H NMR
(CDCl3, 300 MHz) δ 7.28-7.23 (m, 2H), 6.31 (t, 1H, J = 8.8 Hz), 4.23 (q,
2H, J = 7.1 Hz), 3.88 (s, 2H), 1.27 (t, 3H, J = 7.1 Hz); LRMS (FAB) m/z
323 (M + H+). Anal. (C10H11FINO2) C, H, N.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Novel Potent Antagonists of Transient Receptor Potential Channel,
Vanilloid Subfamily Member 1: Structure-Activity Relationship of
