$DATUM 4-(3,4-Dihydro-2H-pyran-5-yl)morpholine (6). A round-bottom flask
equipped with a stir bar, Dean-Strak trap and condenser was charged with
dihydro-2H-pyran-3(4H)-one 5 (6.00 g, 59.9 mmol), morpholine (7.83 g,
89.9 mmol) and toluene (120 mL). This mixture was brought to reflux with
azeotropic removal of water. After about 4 h, the reaction mixture was
concentrated under reduced pressure. The crude product 6 as an oil (10.1
g) and used without purification. This material contained approximately
10% of the undesired regioisomer
4-(5,6-dihydro-2H-pyran-3-yl)-morpholine. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 6.04
(s, 1H), 3.85 (t, J = 4 Hz, 1H), 3.74 (t, J = 4 Hz, 2H), 2.69 (t, J = 4
Hz, 2H), 2.12 (t, J = 8 Hz, 1H), 1.92-1.84 (m, 1H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, Dean-Stark trap used, mixture ratio, 7.5:1
