$DATUM 3-((3S,7R,8R,9αR)-2-Benzyl-7,8-dimethyl-3-phenyl-octahydro-
1H-pyrido[1,2-]pyrazin-8-yl)phenol (8). To a solution of 5α (1 g, 2.98
mmol) in ethanol (20 mL) was added benzaldehyde (0.95 g, 8.93 mmol), and
the reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature for 10 min. To this
was then added BAP (0.82 g, 8.93 mmol), and the reaction mixture was
stirred at room temperature for 18 h. The mixture was concentrated under
reduced pressure. The residue was taken up in ethyl acetate. The mixture
was washed with a saturated aqueous sodium bicarbonate solution, water,
and brine, dried over magnesium sulfate, filtered, and concentrated under
reduced pressure. The crude product was purified by column chromatography
(eluent: dichloromethane/methanol/ammonium hydroxide mixtures of
increasing polarity). Yield 71% (white solid); white solid;1H NMR (CD3OD)
δ 0.76 (d, J = 7 Hz, 3H), 1.31 (s, 3H), 1.38 (d, J = 13 Hz, 1H), 1.89 (t,
J = 13 Hz, 1H), 2.04 (m, 2H), 2.32 (t, J = 11 Hz, 1H), 2.48 (m, 1H), 2.54
(dd, J = 11 and 2 Hz, 1H), 2.69 (t, J = 3 Hz, 1H), 2.72 (t, J = 3 Hz,
1H), 2.79 (dd, J = 11 and 2 Hz, 1H), 2.90 (d, J = 13 Hz, 1H), 3.51 (dd, J
= 10 and 3 Hz, 1H), 3.74 (d, J = 13 Hz, 1H), 6.55 (dd, J = 7 and 1 Hz,
1H), 6.67 (t, J = 2 Hz, 1H), 6.71 (d, J = 7 Hz, 1H), 7.08 (t, J = 8 Hz,
1H), 7.21 (m, 1H), 7.28 (m, 5H), 7.37 (t, J = 8 Hz, 2H), 7.53 (d, J = 6
Hz, 2H); LCMS (ESI) m/z 427 (M + H+). Anal. (C29H34N2O) C, H, N.
