$DATUM N-benzyl-(2S)-pyroglutamic acid (3) N-benzyl-(2S)-pyroglutamic acid 3 was
synthesized from L-glutamic acid 2 (14.7 g, 0.1 mol) and benzaldehyde
(25.4 g, 0.24 mol,) using 2 N NaOH (170 ml) and NaBH4 (1.2 equivalent,
4.6 g, 0.12 mol) accordingly to procedure as described in literature and
obtained. White solid (Peterson et al., 1984). Yield: 15.3 g, 70%.
