$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Exemplary procedure for reductive aminations with dialdehyde 8: A
solution of dialdehyde 8 (0.3809 g, 0.602 mmol) in MeOH (12 mL) was
treated with benzylamine hydrochloride (0.259 g, 1.80 mmol) followed by
NaCNBH3 (0.113 g, 1.80 mmol), and the reaction was stirred at RT, and
progress was monitored by LC/MS. After 7 h, the starting material was
consumed according to LC/MS analysis, and the crude reaction mixture was
loaded directly onto a 12 g C18‐Biotage reverse phase column for
purification (10-100% CH3CN/H2O). Compound 15, white solid, yield 0.2353
g, 55%. m/z [M + H] = 708.
