$DATUM 6-N,N-Bis(2,2,2-trifluoroethyl)amino -4-trifluoromethylquinolin-2(1H)-one
(4m) A 2L round bottom flask, under N2, was charged with a solution of 3
(6.9 g, 74.1mmol) in 200 mL trifluoroacetic acid. NaBH4 pellets (10
pellets, approx 0.2 mol) were added with 30 minutes intervals. The
mixture was stirred at rt for 16h and then heated to 70°C and more NaBH4
pellets (approximately 10, 0.2 mol) were added until no more starting
material or monoalkylated product was visible on TLC. The heating bath
was removed, and water was carefully added while the mixture was still
warm. In total 1 L water was slowly added. The precipitate was filtered
and rinsed with water. The dark solids were dissolved in 600 mL EtOAc and
stirred with 3g activated carbon. Filtered through a short plug of silica
gel, concentrated and crystallized from 650 mL MeOH and 30 mL water to
give 24.0 g (83%) pure 6-N,N-bis(trifluoroethyl)amino-4-
trifluoromethylquinolin-2(1H)-one (4m) as a slightly yellow solid. From
the filtrate a second batch of 4.0 g >95% pure
6-N,N-bis(2,2,2-trifluoroethyl)amino-4-trifluoromethylquinolin-2(1H)-one
(4m) was isolated. 1H NMR(500 MHz, DMSO-d 6 ) : δ 12.2 (bs, 1 H), 7.58
(dd, 1H, J = 9.3, 2.7), 7.39 (d, 1H, J = 9.3), 7.16 (s, 1 H), 6.98 (s, 1
H), 4.39 (q, 4H, J = 9.0).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of
6-N,N-Bis(2,2,2-trifluoroethyl)amino-4-trifluoromethylquinolin-2(1H)-one
as a Novel Selective Androgen Receptor Modulator
