$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Allyl 4-(phenethylamino)piperidine-1-carboxylate (12).
N-Alloc-4-piperidone 11 (0.51 g 2.8 mmol) was dissolved in methanol (5
mL); phenethylamine (0.4 mL, 3 mmol) and glacial acetic acid (5 drops)
were added. The reaction mixture was stirred at rt for 1 h. Sodium
borohydride (0.113 mg, 3 mmol) dissolved in methanol (5 mL) was added
dropwise over 5 min. The reaction mixture was stirred for an additional 2
h at rt, and the solvent was evaporated under reduced pressure. The
resultant oil was purified by column chromatography using 20% ethyl
acetate/heptane as eluant to give 12 (0.3 g, 40%). 1H NMR (250 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 7.25-7.12 (m, 5H), 5.85 (tdd, J = 17.2, 10.4, 5.9 Hz, 1H), 5.21
(qd, J = 17.2, 1.5 Hz, 1H), 5.12 (qd, J = 10.4, 1.4 Hz, 1H), 4.50 (td, J
= 5.4, 1.4, 2H), 2.94-2.67 (m, 8H), 2.63-2.50 (m 1H), 1.83-1.73 (m, 2H),
1.27-1.00 (m, 2H); MS (ES+): m/z = 289 [M + H]+.
