$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of (2S,3S)-2-Aminopentane-1,3-diol.
(S)-1,3-Dihydroxypentan-2-one (2.36 g; 0.5 M in water, 40 mL) was added
to a solution of isopropylamine (1.25 mL; 6.7 M in water, 4.54 mL, pH
7.5) in 1 M HEPES (23.3.mL, pH 7.5) containing and pyridoxal 5'-phosphate
hydrate (17.1 mg, 69 μmol) To this mixture was further added water (165.5
mL) and clarified CV2025 ω-TAm lysate (100 mL). Lysate was obtained in
100 mM HEPES, pH 7.5, containing 0.2 mM PLP, 0.5 mM phenylmethyl sulfonyl
fluoride (PMSF), and 8 U of benzonase (Novagen)/ mL of cell extract. The
reaction was shaken in a 500 mL Erlenmeyer flask at 100 rpm and 37°C for
48 h and monitored exclusively by LC-MS. The enzyme was spun down (4500
rpm, at 4°C for 10 min), and the mixture was additionally filtered
through a 0.2 μm sterile filter. Amberlite IRA-410 resin (50 g) was added
to the reaction mixture. After 1 h, the resin was removed by filtration
and washed with H2O (300 mL). The aqueous mixture was then passed through
an Isolute SCX-2 (Biotage) ionexchange column (40 g of resin) and the
column washed with MeOH (2 × 200 mL). The column was then eluted with 4 M
NH3 in MeOH (3 × 200 mL) and the eluent concentrated to yield the desired
product as a solid (410 mg, 26%). The ee of the (2S,3S)-product was
determined to be >98% (S-isomer at C-2) and the de determined as 61% by
chiral HPLC, the impurity being exclusively
(2S,3R)-2-aminopentane-1,3-diol. (2S,3S)-2-Aminopentane-1,3-diol, yield
(410 mg, 26%). Found (+HRCI) MH+, 120.10250; C5H14NO2 requires 120.10245;
1H NMR (500 MHz; D2O): δ 0.93 (2.4H, t, J 7.5, CH3), 0.94 (0.6H, t, J
6.5, CH3), 1.40-1.60 (2H, m, CH2CH3), 2.76 (0.8H, ddd, J 6.3, 5.1, and
4.6, CHNH2), 2.81 (0.4H, ddd, J 7.5, 5.9, and 4.1, CHNH2), 3.47-3.76 (3H,
m, CH2OH and CHOH);13C NMR (75 MHz; H2O): δ (2S,3S) 10.1, 26.3, 55.8,
64.1,73.7; (2S,3R) 9.9, 25.6, 56.2, 63.7, 74.7.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM biotransformation, enzymic, stereoselective, optimization study,
recombinant omega-transaminase (CV2025) from Chromobacterium violaceum
(DSM30191) expressed in Escherichia coli and benzonase used, HEPES
buffered solution used, scale up, subsequent treatment with Amberlite
IRA-410 resin, optimized on cosolvent and substrate ratio
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A Multidisciplinary Approach Toward the Rapid and Preparative-Scale
Biocatalytic Synthesis of Chiral Amino Alcohols: A Concise
Transketolase-/ω-Transaminase-Mediated Synthesis of
(2S,3S)-2-Aminopentane-1,3-diol
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Smith, Mark E. B.; Chen, Bing H.; Hibbert, Edward G.; Kaulmann, Ursula;
Smithies, Kirsty; Galman, James L.; Baganz, Frank; Dalby, Paul A.;
Hailes, Helen C.; Lye, Gary J.; Ward, John M.; Woodley, John M.;
Micheletti, Martina
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Process Research & Development (2010), 14(1), 99-107

