$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Di-tert-butyl
[1-(3,5-difluorophenyl)ethyl]imidodicarbonate. To a solution of
[1-(3,5-difluorophenyl)ethyl]amine (10.0 g, 63.6 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (180 mL)
at 0 °C was added di-tertbutyl dicarbonate (15.3 g, 70.0 mmol) and the
resulting mixture was stirred at ambient temperature for 1 h. The solvent
was removed under reduced pressure. To the residue was added
di-tert-butyl dicarbonate (20.8 g, 95.4 mmol) and DMAP (1.94 g, 15.9
mmol) and the reaction mixture was heated at 80 °C for 2 h. Additional
di-tert-butyl dicarbonate (2.78 g, 12.7 mmol) was added and the reaction
mixture was heated at 80 °C for 1 h. The reaction mixture was allowed to
cool, and was concentrated in vacuo. The crude product was purified by
silica gel chromatography, eluting with a gradient of hexane:EtOAc -
100:0 to 85:15, to give the title compound (21.9 g, 96%). tert-Butyl
2-[(tert-butoxycarbonyl)amino]-2-(3,5-difluorophenyl)propanoate (17). To
a stirred suspension of potassium tert-butoxide (64 g, 570 mmol) in THF
(800 mL) at -78 °C was added a solution of di-tert-butyl
[1-(3,5-difluorophenyl)ethyl]imidodicarbonate (68 g, 190 mmol) in THF
(480 mL), dropwise, over 45 min. The reaction mixture was allowed to warm
to ambient temperature and stirring was continued for 1 h. The reaction
mixture was cooled to -78 °C and quenched with 1 N aqueous HCl (600 mL),
warmed to 0 °C, and poured into Et2O (750 mL). The organic layer was
extracted and the aqueous layer was extracted further with Et2O (750 mL).
The combined organic extracts were dried over Na2SO4, filtered, and
concentrated in vacuo. The crude product was purified by silica gel
chromatography, eluting with hexane:EtOAc - 100:0 to 80:20, to give the
title compound (35 g, 52%). tert-Butyl
[1-(3,5-difluorophenyl)-1-methy2-oxoethyl]carbamate (18). To a stirred
solution of tert-butyl
2-[(tert-butoxycarbonyl)amino]-2-(3,5-difluorophenyl)propanoate (27.0 g,
76 mmol) in THF (350 mL) at -78 °C was added LiA4 (76 mL of a 1 M
solution in THF, 76 mmol), dropwise. The reaction mixture was stirred at
-78 °C for 3 h, then quenched by successive addition of EtOAc (76 mL),
H2O (228 mL), 1 N aqueous NaOH (76 mL), and EtOAc (228 mL). The reaction
mixture was warmed to ambient temperature, stirred for 1 h, filtered, and
extracted with EtOAc (2 X 450 mL). The organic extracts were dried over
Na2SO4, filtered, and concentrated in vacuo. The crude product was
purified by silica gel chromatography, eluting with hexane:EtOAc - 100:0
to 70:30, to give the title compound as an oil which solidifies on
standing (16.8 g, 78%). Methyl
1-{[2-[(tert-butoxycarbonyl)amino]-2-(3,5-difluorophenyl)propyl]amino}cyclopentanecarboxylate
(19). To a stirred solution of tert-butyl
[1-(3,5-difluorophenyl)-1-methy2-oxoethyl]carbamate (1.90 g, 6.66 mmol)
in MeOH (25 mL) were added methyl 1-aminocyclopentanecarboxylate (9.54 g,
66.6 mmol) and glacial acetic acid (3.81 mL, 67 mmol) and the reaction
mixture was stirred at ambient temperature for 30 min. To this stirred
solution was added NaCNBH3 (0.628 g, 9.99 mmol) and the solution was
adjusted to pH = 5 with glacial acetic acid. After stirring for 30 min,
the reaction mixture was poured into saturated aqueous NaHCO3 (50 mL) and
extracted with CH2Cl2 (3 X 100 mL). The combined organic extracts were
washed with brine, dried over Na2SO4, filtered, and concentrated in
vacuo. The crude product was purified by silica gel chromatography,
eluting with hexane:EtOAc - 100:0 to 50:50, to give the title compound
(1.64 g, 60%).
(8R)-8-(3,5-Difluorophenyl)-8-methy6,9-diazaspiro[4.5]decan-10-one
[(R)-20]. A solution of methyl
1-{[2-[(tert-butoxycarbonyl)amino]-2-(3,5-difluorophenyl)propyl]amino}
cyclopentanecarboxylate (1.60 g, 3.88 mmol) in EtOAc was stirred at 0 °C
and HCl gas was bubbled into the solution for 2 min. The reaction mixture
was stirred for 30 min at 0 °C and then poured carefully into saturated
aqueous NaHCO3 (30 mL) and extracted with EtOAc (2 X 50 mL). The combined
organic extracts were dried over Na2SO4, filtered, and concentrated in
vacuo to give the deprotected intermediate (1.20 g, 99%). To a solution
of the deprotected intermediate (1.20 g, 3.84 mmol) in xylenes (25 mL)
was added glacial HOAc (2.4 mL, 42 mmol) and the reaction mixture was
heated at 80 °C for 3 h. The cooled mixture was poured into saturated
aqueous NaHCO3 (20 mL) and extracted with EtOAc (2 X 50 mL). The combined
organic extracts were dried over Na2SO4, filtered, and concentrated under
reduced pressure. The crude product was purified by silica gel
chromatography, eluting with a gradient of EtOAc:MeOH - 100:0: to 92:8,
to give the racemic titled compound (970 mg, 90%). The enantiomers were
separated by HPLC, using a ChiralPak AD column and eluting with
hexane:EtOH:Et2NH - 40:60:0.1. The first major peak to elute was
(8S)-8-(3,5-difluorophenyl)-8-methy6,9-diazaspiro[4.5]decan-10-one and
the second major peak to elute was
(8R)-8-(3,5-difluorophenyl)-8-methy6,9-diazaspiro[4.5]decan-10-one, the
title compound. Ethyl
[(8R)-8-(3,5-difluorophenyl)-8-methy10-oxo-6,9-diazaspiro[4.5]dec-9-yl]acetate.
To a stirred solution of (8R)-8-(3,5-difluorophenyl)-8-methy6,9-
diazaspiro[4.5]decan-10-one (195 mg, 0.70 mmol) in THF (5 mL) at 0 °C was
added NaH (31 mg of a 60% dispersion in oil, 0.77 mmol). After 5 min,
ethyl bromoacetate (128 mg, 0.77 mmol) was added and the mixture was
allowed to warm to ambient temperature and stirring was continued for 1
h. The mixture was cooled in an ice-water bath, saturated aqueous NaHCO3
(10 mL) was added and the mixture was extracted with EtOAc (2 X 20 mL).
The combined organic layers were dried over Na2SO4, filtered, and
concentrated in vacuo. The crude product was purified by silica gel
chromatography, eluting with a gradient of CH2Cl2:EtOAc - 100:0 to 0:100,
to give the title compound (222 mg, 87%).
[(8R)-8-(3,5-Difluorophenyl)-8-methy10-oxo-6,9-diazaspiro[4.5]dec-9-yl]acetic
acid (21). To a solution of ethyl
[(8R)-8-(3,5-difluorophenyl)-8-methy10-oxo-6,9-
diazaspiro[4.5]dec-9-yl]acetate (2.09 g, 5.69 mmol) in THF (15 mL) and
H2O (5 mL) was added 1 N aqueous LiOH (6.83 mL, 6.83 mmol), followed by
sufficient EtOH (1-2 mL) to make the mixture homogeneous, and the
resulting mixture was stirred at ambient temperature for 18 h. The
organic solvents were removed under reduced pressure and the resulting
mixture was acidified by addition of 1 N HCl. The precipitate was
isolated by filtration and dried to give the title compound (1.83 g,
95%).
2-[(8R)-8-(3,5-Difluorophenyl)-8-methy10-oxo-6,9-diazaspiro[4.5]dec-9-yl]-N-[(2R)-2'-oxo-1,1',2',3-tetrahydrospiro[indene-2,3'-pyrrolo[2,3-b]pyridin]-5-yl]acetamide
(7). To a mixture of
[(8R)-8-(3,5-difluorophenyl)-8-methy10-oxo-6,9-diazaspiro[4.5]dec-9-yl]acetic
acid (3.25 g, 9.61 mmol),
(R)-5-amino-1,3-dihydrospiro[indene-2,3'-pyrrolo[2,3-
b]pyridin]-2'(1'H)-one20 (2.53 g, 10.09 mmol), and HATU (4.38 g, 11.53
mmol) in DMF (30 mL) was added N-methylmorpholine (2.11 mL, 19.2 mmol)
and the resulting mixture was stirred at ambient temperature for 2 h. The
reaction mixture was diluted with EtOAc (1 L) and washed successively
with saturated aqueous NaHCO3 (250 mL), and brine (250 mL). The organic
layer was dried over Na2SO4, filtered, and concentrated in vacuo. The
residue was purified by silica gel chromatography, eluting with
CH2Cl2:MeOH - 100:0 to 90:10, to give the title compound (5.49 g, 68%).
2-((R)-8-(3,5-Difluorophenyl)-6,8-dimethy10-oxo-6,9-diazaspiro[4.5]decan-9-yl)-N-((S)-2'-oxo-1',2',5,7-tetrahydrospiro[cyclopenta[b]pyridine-6,3'-pyrrolo[2,3-b]pyridin]-3-yl)acetamide
(9). Compound 9 was prepared in an analogous manner to compound 8 except
using
(S)-3-amino-5,7-dihydrospiro[cyclopenta[b]pyridine-6,3'-pyrrolo[2,3-b]pyridin]-2'(1'H)-
one (U.S. Patent 7,625,901) in place of
(R)-5-amino-1,3-dihydrospiro[indene-2,3'-pyrrolo[2,3-
b]pyridin]-2'(1'H)-one.20 1H NMR (CD3OD): δ 8.53 (1H, s); 8.09 (1H, dd, J
= 8.8, 6.8 Hz); 8.02 (1H, s); 7.32 (1H, dd, J = 7.3, 1.5 Hz); 7.03 (2H, J
= 9.0, 2.2 Hz ); 6.96 (1H, dd, J = 7.3, 5.4 Hz ); 6.91 (1H, dt, J = 8.8,
2.2 Hz); 4.19 (1H, d, J = 16.1 Hz); 3.60 (1H, d, J = 16.1 Hz); 3.52 (2H,
d, J = 16.4 Hz); 3.25-3.18 (2H, m); 2.95 (1H, d, J = 12.9 Hz); 2.81 (1H,
d, J = 12.7 Hz); 2.24-2.18 (1H, m); 2.23 (3H, s); 2.09-1.94 (3H, m);
1.84-1.78 (2H, m); 1.79 (3H, s); 1.74-1.72 (2H, m). MS: m/z = 587 (M +1).
HPLC purity data acquired on a Waters 2695 Separations Module with a YMC
Pro C18 column (3 X 50 mm, 5 μ, 120 Å), eluting with a gradient of
ACN:H2O 8:92 to 100:0 (0.05% TFA) over 3.3 min: rt = 1.39 min (99% purity
at 215).
