$DATUM (R)-1-(2-methylcyclopentyl)pyrrolidin-3-ol (40) Procedure adaptated from
ref. 2-methylcyclopentanone (3.7 mL, 34.8 mmol) and (R)-3-pyrrolidinol
(0.940 g, 10.8 mmol) were dissolved in 15 mL of MeOH with AcOH (per 100
mL of MeOH add 6 μL AcOH). Molecular sieves 3 Å were added. When cooling
down to 0 °C the reaction turned pink. After 5 minutes a solution of
NaBH3CN (1.10 g, 17.5 mmol) in MeOH (5 mL) was added to the reaction. The
solution was stirred 14 hours, warming slowly up to room temperature. The
reaction was filtered, quenched adding NaOH 1M followed by extraction
with CH2Cl2 . The organics were dried over Na2SO4, filtered, concentrated
to dryness, and the residue was purified by column chromatography
(neutral alumina, AcOEt-AcOEt/MeOH 1%). a colorless oil (0.974 g, 54%
yield). 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz) diastereomeric mixture (1:1) δ 4.38-4.29
(m, 1H), 4.09 (br s, 1H), 3.04-2.90 (m, 1H), 2.85-2.74 (m, 1H), 2.73-2.54
(m, 1H), 2.52-2.35 (m, 2H), 2.26-2.04 (m, 2H), 1.86-1.49 (m, 6H),
1.47-1.32 (m, 1H), 0.89 (d, J= 7 Hz, 1.5H), 0.88 (d, J= 7 Hz, 1.5H); 13C
NMR (CDCl3, 75 MHz) diastereomeric mixture (1:1) δ 71.1 (CH), 71.0 (CH),
70.2 (CH), 70.1 (CH), 52.3 (CH2), 52.2 (CH2), 36.0 (CH), 35.9 (CH), 34.7
(CH2), 34.6 (CH2), 31.4 (CH2), 31.3 (CH2), 28.0 (CH2), 27.9 (CH2), 20.4
(CH2), 20.3 (CH2), 14.1 (CH3), 14.0 (CH3); MS (ESI+) m/z 170.6 ([[M+1]+).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM modified literature procedure, mol. sieves used, 1:1 dr
