$DATUM (1S,2R)-2-Methyl-N-((S)-1-phenylethyl)cyclopentanamine (18a). A mixture
of 2-methylcyclopentanone (0.294 g, 3.0 mmol), (S)-1-phenylethanamine
(0.774 mL, 6.0 mmol), and a catalytic amount of TsOH in benzene (25 mL)
was refluxed overnight. After being cooled to room temperature, the
reaction mixture was diluted with 10 mL of absolute EtOH, and sodium
cyanoborohydride (569 mg, 9 mmol) was then added to the reaction mixture
in three portions over a ∼5 h period. The reaction mixture was quenched
with brine (50 mL), partitioned with ethyl acetate (50 mL), dried over
MgSO4, and concentrated on reduced pressure. The resulting residue was
subjected to silica gel chromatography. The major component as 18a (0.238
g, 36%). 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.49-7.04 (m, 5H), 3.78 (q, J = 6.6
Hz, 1H), 2.82 (m, 1H), 2.10 (m, 1H), 1.74-1.56 (m, 3H), 1.46-1.35 (m,
1H), 1.33 (d, J = 6.5 Hz, 3H), 1.28 (m, 2H), 0.87 (d, J = 7.0 Hz, 3H);
13C NMR (126 MHz, CDCl3) δ 146.29, 128.30, 126.72, 126.67, 59.51, 56.26,
34.02, 31.51, 30.18, 24.99, 20.25, 13.56. MS (ESI): calculated for
C14H21N [M + H]+, 204.18; found, 204.14.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective (in stage 1)
