$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM A solution of (2-chloro-3-fluorophenyl)methanamine 17 (1.87 g, 11.72
mmol), 1,2-dichloroethane (39.1 mL), pyruvic aldehyde dimethyl acetal
(1.387 mL, 11.72 mmol), and sodium triacetoxyborohydride (3.48 g, 16.4
mmol) was stirred at ambient temperature. After 16 h, 2 N NaOH (100 mL)
was added and stirred until the organic layer was almost clear (30 min,
cloudy early on). The layers were separated, and the aqueous layer was
extracted with DCM (50 mL), dried (Na2SO4), and concentrated, giving
crude N-(2-chloro-3-fluorobenzyl)-1,1-dimethoxypropan-2-amine. Yield
(3.04 g, 11.62 mmol, 99%).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Pomeranz-Fritsch Reaction (Schlittler-Muller Modification)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of
(R)-1-(7-Chloro-2,2-bis(fluoromethyl)chroman-4-yl)-3-(3-methylisoquinolin-5-yl)urea
(A-1165442): A Temperature-Neutral Transient Receptor Potential
Vanilloid-1 (TRPV1) Antagonist with Analgesic Efficacy
