$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-[Benzyl(3-methyl-4-nitrobutyl)amino]ethanol (17). To a solution of
3-methyl-4-nitrobutyraldehyde 16 (0.73 g, 5.57 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (6.0 mL)
were added sodium triacetoxyborohydride (1.57 g, 7.40 mmol) and
N-benzylethanolamine (0.55 g, 3.67 mmol) at room temperature. The
reaction was stirred for 16 h, whereupon it was quenched with water,
diluted with EtOAc, and washed with aqueous NaHCO3 and brine. The organic
layer was dried over sodium sulfate, concentrated, and used directly in
the next reaction: 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 7.41-7.29 (m, 6H), 4.29-4.19 (m, 2H),
3.69-3.59 (m, 4H), 2.79-2.31 (m, 4H), 1.61-1.39 (m, 4H), 0.97 (d, J = 6.9
Hz, 3H); MS (ESI) 265.3 (M + H)+.
