$DATUM Ethyl
2-methyl-2-(4-(4-(2-(4-methylbenzyl)hydrazinyl)-4-oxobutyl)phenoxy)propanoate
hydrochloride (48). Carboxylic acid 5 (120.00 g, 407.7 mmol, 1.0 equiv)
was dissolved in toluene (1.2 L) and DMF (0.32 mL, 4.08 mmol, 0.10 equiv)
was added. To the stirred solution was added oxalyl chloride (48.5 mL,
555 mmol, 1.36 equiv) at a rate to control off gassing. The reaction
mixture was stirred at rt for 1.5 h and was then concentrated via rotary
evaporation to give an oil (127.5 g). Toluene (127.5 g) was added to give
a 1/1 solution of acid chloride and toluene stock solution. tert-Butyl
hydrazinecarboxylate (12.0 g, 90.7 mmol, 1.00 equiv) was dissolved in a
mixture of EtOAc (213 mL) and pyridine (16.90 mL, 208.6 mmol, 2.30
equiv). The solution was cooled in an ice bath to 0-5 °C and a solution
of the acid chloride above (56.75 g of solution, 28.37 g of acid
chloride, 90.7 mmol, 1.0 equiv) was added and the reaction was warmed to
rt, resulting in a thick slurry. The reaction was stirred for 1 h at rt
and was then washed sequentially with 1 N HCl (2 × 200 mL), saturated
NaHCO3 solution (200 mL), and brine (200 mL). The organic fraction was
dried over magnesium sulfate, filtered and concentrated via rotary
evaporation to give an oil (38.87 g). The oil was dissolved in EtOAc (500
mL) and HCl gas was sparged through the solvent for 15 min. The solution
was stirred at rt for 2 h then was concentrated to approximately ½ total
volume. The resultant slurry was cooled to 0-5 °C overnight and filtered.
The cake was washed with diethyl ether (2 × 100 mL). The resultant solid
was dried in vacuo to give a solid (27.83 g). The solid from above (27.57
g, 79.95 mmol, 1.00 equiv) was dissolved in dioxane (400 mL) and
paratolualdehyde (9.61 g, 79.95 mmol, 1.00 equiv) was added. The reaction
was concentrated via rotary evaporation at 60 °C to give a yellow gel.
This gel was concentrated from EtOH (200 mL) to give a solid (35.01 g).
The solid (35.0 g, 85.3 mmol, 1.00 equiv) was dissolved in isopropyl
alcohol (220 mL) and AcOH (107 mL). To the solution was added 5% Pt/C
(50% H2O wet, 4.16 g, 21.8 mmol, 0.25 equiv) and the system was
pressurized to 50 psi hydrogen at 50 °C for 3 h. The reaction was
filtered across Celite® filter aid and the cake was washed with IPA (50
mL × 2). The filtrate was concentrated via rotary evaporation to an oil.
The oil was concentrated from EtOAc (100 mL). EtOAc (43 mL) and Et2O (439
mL) were added to the resultant oil to give a thin white suspension.
Hydrogen chloride gas was sparged through the system for 15 min, giving a
slurry. The slurry was cooled in an ice bath for 30 min. The slurry was
filtered and the cake was washed with cold diethyl ether (2 × 20 mL). The
solid was dried in vacuo to give the product (23.03 g, 57 % from toluene
solution of intermediate) as a white solid Ethyl
2-methyl-2-(4-(4-(2-(4-methylbenzyl)hydrazinyl)-4-oxobutyl)phenoxy)propanoate
hydrochloride (48). Yield (23.03 g, 57 %). mp 102-105 °C. 1H NMR
(DMSO-d6): δ 1.13 (t, J = 7.3 Hz, 3H), 1.45 (s, 6H), 1.61 (m, 2H), 2.10
(t, J = 7.3 Hz, 2H), 2.21 (s, 3H), 2.27-2.30 (m, 2H), 4.12 (q, J = 7.1
Hz, 2H), 4.16 (s, 2H), 6.67 (m, 2H), 6.96 (m, 2H), 7.13 (m, 2H), 7.36 (m,
2H), 11.40 (s, 1H); 13C NMR (DMSO-d6): δ 14.3, 21.1, 25.4 (2C), 26.8,
32.7, 33.7, 52.7, 61.4, 79.0, 119.2 (2C), 127.6 (2C), 129.3 (2C), 129.5
(2C), 131.2, 135.4, 138.1, 138.9, 153.5, 171.2, 173.7; IR (ATR): 3125,
2966, 2671, 2562, 1731, 1684, 1608, 1507 cm-1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM gaseous HCl used
