$DATUM 4-Methyl-2-[(thiophen-2-ylmethylene)-amino]-pentanoic acid tert-butyl
ester To a stirred solution of leucine t-butyl ester hydrochloride (2 g,
0.89 mmol) in DCM (10 mL) was added thiophene-2-carboxaldehyde (1.0 g,
0.89 mmol) in dry DCM (10 mL). Triethylamine (1.23 mL, 0.90 mL) was added
and the mixture heated to 50°Cfor 4.5 hours. The mixture was cooled,
washed with water (50 mL), dried over magnesium sulfate, filtered, and
evaporated give a white solid (2.48 g, 99%). The imine contains ca. 18%
of thiophene-2-carboxaldehyde and was used directly in the next step. 1H
NMR (CDCl3): δ 8.38 (1H, s), 7.42 (1H, dd), 7.35 (1H, dd), 7.08 (1H, d),
3.94 (1H, dd), 1.86-1.71 (2H, m), 1.65-1.57 (1H, m), 1.46 (9H, s), 0.94
(3H, d), 0.89 (3H, d).
