$DATUM (R)-t-Butyl-(3-(4-((thiophen-3-ylmethyl)amino)piperidin-1-yl)butyl)carbamate
(8). A solution of thiophene 3-methylamine 7 (6.27 g, 55.3 mmol),
intermediate 6 (13.52 g, 50.3 mmol), NaBH(OAc)3 (14.92 g, 70.3 mmol) and
acetic acid (2.9 mL, 50.3 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (250 mL) was stirred at room
temperature for 18 h. The reaction mixture was quenched with aqueous
saturated NaHCO3 solution (250 mL) and extracted with CH2Cl2 (2 X 150
mL). The organic layers were combined, dried (Na2SO4), filtered and
concentrated. The crude material was purified by column chromatography
(CH2Cl2/MeOH/NH4OH, 90:10:1, v/v/v) to afford 8. 8 (16.0 g, 86%) as a
yellow oil 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 0.96 (d, J= 6.6 Hz, 3H), 1.43 (s,
9H), 1.59-2.29 (m, 4H), 2.31-2.65 (m, 2H), 2.69-2.89 (s, 3H), 2.96-3.37
(m, 2H), 3.48 (s, 4H), 3.86 (s, 2H), 5.91 (s, 1H), 7.05 (d, J= 4.9 Hz,
1H), 7.15 (s, 1H), 7.29 (dd, J= 4.9, 3.0 Hz, 1H).
