$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Step1:
4-[2-(ethoxycarbonyl)-8-{[4-(4-phenylbutoxy)benzoyl]amino}-2,3-dihydro-4H-1,4-benzoxazin-4-yl]butanoic
acid (8-2) Under atmosphere of argon, to a solution of 8 (2.00 g, 4.22
mmol), 4-oxobutanoic acid (474 mg, 4.64 mmol) and acetic acid (608 mg,
12.7 mmol) in EtOH (20.0 mL) and THF (20.0 mL) was added 10%
palladium-carbon (50 w/w %, hydroscopic, 200 mg), and the mixture was
stirred for 21 hours under atmosphere of hydrogen at room temperature.
The catalyst was filtered off and the filtrate was concentrated. The
residue was recrystallized from a mixed solvent of i-PrOH and n-hexane to
give 8-2 (1.73 g, 73%).
8-{[4-(4-phenylbutoxy)benzoyl]amino}-3,4-dihydro-2H-1,4-benzoxazine-2-carboxylic
acid (1) To a mixture of 8 (200 mg, 0.42 mmol), THF (1.0 mL) and EtOH
(1.0 mL) was added 2 mol/L aqueous solution of sodium hydroxide (1.0 mL),
and the mixture was stirred for 1 hour at room temperature. The reaction
mixture was acidified with 2 mol/L hydrochloric acid and extracted with
EtOAc. The organic layer was washed sequentially with water and saturated
brine, dried over anhydrous sodium sulfate and concentrated. The residue
was recrystallized from EtOH to give 1 (143 mg, 76%).
4-(5-carboxypentyl)-8-{[4-(4-phenylbutoxy)benzoyl]amino}-3,4-dihydro-2H-1,4-benzoxazine-2-carboxylic
acid (11c), yield 88%. 1H NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 1.23-1.33 (m, 2H),
1.44-1.56 (m, 4H), 1.68-1.78(m, 4H), 2.19 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H), 2.63 (t, J
= 6.9 Hz, 2H), 3.12-3.54 (m, 4H), 4.05 (t, J = 5.4 Hz, 2H), 4.97 (t, J =
3.3 Hz, 1H), 6.52 (dd, J = 8.4 Hz, 1.2 Hz, 1H), 6.75 (t, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H),
7.02 (d, J = 9.0 Hz, 2H), 7.12-7.30 (m, 6H), 7.86 (d, J = 9.0 Hz, 2H),
9.16 (s, 1H), 12.47 (brs, 1H). MS (FAB, Neg.) m/z 559 (M - H)- . HRMS
(FAB, Neg.) C32H36N2O7 (M - H)-calc. mass 559.2444, found 559.2449.
