$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Sodium triacetoxyborohydride (4.79 g. 22.6 mmol) was added to a solution
of t-butyl 4-oxopiperidine-1-carboxylate (3.0 g, 15.1 mmol) and
5-aminopyrimidine (1.58 g, 16.6 mmol) in dichloroethane (15 mL) and the
mixture heated under reflux overnight. After cooling to room temperature,
ethyl acetate was added (50 mL), the mixture washed with 2M NaOH(aq) (3 x
50 mL), brine (50 mL) and the organic phase separated, dried (MgSO4),
filtered and the filtrate was concentrated under vacuum. Purified by
column chromatography (Flashmaster II) (eluent 0-10% methanol in
dichloromethane). The solid obtained was triturated with diethyl ether to
give t-butyl 4-(pyrimidin-5-ylamino)piperidine-1-carboxylate. Orange
solid, yield 1.3 g, 31%.
