$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: tert-Butyl
(3-((tert-Butoxycarbonyl)amino)propyl)(3-(cyclopentadecylamino)propyl)carbamate
(10a). A solution of diBoc-norspermidine 9a 8b (410 mg, 1.2 mmol) in
CH2Cl2 (10 mL) was added dropwise to a solution of cyclopentadecanone 8
(250 mg, 1.1 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (10 mL) and allowed to stir at room
temperature for 10 min. Sodium triacetoxyborohydride (1.2 g, 5.6 mmol)
and acetic acid (67 mg, 1.1 mmol) were then added to the solution and
allowed to stir at room temperature overnight. The reaction was complete
by 1H NMR, and the solution was then washed with aqueous Na2CO3. The
organic layer was separated, dried over anhydrous Na2SO4, filtered, and
concentrated in vacuo. After column chromatography ((70% hexanes/24%
CHCl3/5.9% EtOH/ 0.1% NH4OH)). tert-Butyl
(4-((tert-Butoxycarbonyl)amino)butyl)(4-(cyclopentadecylamino)butyl)carbamate
(10b). A similar procedure as described for 10a was used for 10b except
that Boc-protected polyamine 9b 8a was used. 10b (1.54 g, 54%). 1H NMR
(CDCl3) δ 3.18 (m, 6H), 2.59 (m, 2H), 2.52 (m, 1H), 1.55 (m, 4H),
1.51−1.22 (m, 46H); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 156.0, 155.5, 79.1, 77.3, 56.8,
47.1, 46.5, 40.2, 32.7, 28.5, 28.4, 27.7, 27.5, 27.4, 26.8, 26.6, 26.5,
26.2, 25.9, 25.5, 23.6. HRMS (FAB) m/z calcd for C33H65N3O4 (M)+
568.4975, found 568.5048.
