$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 3-{[3-(1,1,2,2-Tetrafluoroethoxy)benzyl]amino}-phenol (11). To a solution
of 3-aminophenol (4.91 g, 45.0 mmol) and
3-(1,1,2,2-tetrafluoroethoxy)benzaldehyde (10.0 g, 45.0 mmol) dissolved
in 100 mL of 1,2-dichloroethane were added sodium triacetoxyborohydride
(14.28 g 67.5 mmol) and glacial acetic acid (2.7 mL, 47.3 mmol). The
reaction mixture was stirred for 6 h, water was added, and the mixture
was extracted with dichloromethane. The organics were washed with
saturated aqueous sodium bicarbonate then dried over anhyd MgSO4. The
dried organic layer was evaporated to give 11 (11.00 g, 78%) as a dark
orange oil, that was used below without further purification.
3-{[3-(1,1,2,2-Tetrafluoroethoxy)benzyl]amino}-phenol (11), yield (11.00
g, 78%). 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.33 (t, 1H), 7.24-7.27 (m, 2H), 7.11
(dd, 1H), 7.00 (t, 1H), 6.17- 6.22 (m, 2H), 6.08 (t, 1H), 5.88 (tt, 1H),
4.32 (s, 2H). HRMS calcd for C15H14F4NO2 316.0960 [M + H]+, found
316.0989.
