$DATUM 9-(3-Furylmethyl)-3-methylene-1,5-bis(p-toluenesulfonyl)-1,5,9-triazacyclododecane
(10). A solution of 0.11 g (0.20 mmol) of 94-129, 0.15 mL (0.16 g, 1.7
mmol) of 3-furaldehyde, and 39 mg (0.63 mmol) of sodium cyanoborohydride
in 20 mL of methanol was stirred at room temperature for 20 h, producing
a pale yellow precipitate. Filtration and recrystallization from
chloroform/hexane gave 78 mg (68%) of 10 as white crystals, mp
139.5-140.5 °C. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.67 (d, J = 8 Hz, 4 H, o-Ts),
7.32 (d, J = 8 Hz, 4 H, m-Ts), 7.31 (s, 1 H, 2-furyl), 7.21 (bs, 1 H,
5-furyl), 6.17 (bs, 1 H, 4-furyl), 5.17 (s, 2 H, C=CH2), 3.82 (s, 4 H,
H2, H4), 3.27 (s, 2 H, CH2Ar), 3.12 (t, J = 6 Hz, 4 H, H6, H12), 2.44 (s,
6 H, ArCH3), 2.35 (m, 4 H, H8, H10), 1.66 (m, 4 H, H7, H11). 13C NMR (75
MHz, CDCl3) δ 143.6, 143.3, 140.7, 138.9, 136.2, 130.0, 127.6, 122.2,
116.2, 111.3, 51.5, 49.7, 48.4, 44.2, 25.1, 21.7. IR (KBr) 2930 (w), 2822
(w), 1589 (m), 1441 (m), 1336 (s), 1169 (s), 1083 (s), 1037 (m), 877 (m),
819 (s), 730 (s). MS (FAB) m/z 572 (MH+). Anal. Calcd for C29H37N3O5S2:
C, 60.92; H, 6.52; N, 7.35. Found: C, 60.53; H, 6.49; N, 7.09.
