triacetoxyborohydride (0.465 g, 1.5 equiv) was added. After stirring for
1 h, the mixture was diluted with CH2Cl2 and washed with saturated
aqueous NaHCO3, dried (MgSO4), and concentrated to give 28.
N-((1s,4s)-4-(2-(4'-(((3S,5R)-3,5-Dimethylpiperazin-1-yl)methyl)bipheny3-yloxy)-5-
fluoronicotinamido)cyclohexyl)-2-methylthiazole-4-carboxamide 9e.
Prepared from 42 using General Method D, as the trifluoroacetic acid salt
in 50% yield. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3, δ): 8.38 (dd, J = 8.2, 3.1 Hz, 1H),
8.08 (d, J = 3.1 Hz, 1H), 8.03 (d, J = 6.9 Hz, 1H), 7.91 (s, 1H), 7.65 -
7.48 (m, 4H), 7.44 (d, J = 8.2 Hz, 2H), 7.37 (s, 1H), 7.24 - 7.17 (m,
2H), 4.28 - 4.19 (m, 1H), 4.14 - 3.97 (m, 3H), 3.72 - 3.61 (m, 2H), 3.35
- 3.17 (m, 2H), 3.08 - 2.96 (m, 2H), 2.64 (s, 3H), 2.00 - 1.74 (m, 6H),
1.73 - 1.56 (m, 2H), 1.32 (d, J = 6.5 Hz, 6H). LRMS: m/z 657 [M+H]+ Anal.
calcd for C36H41FN6O3S·2C2HF3O2·0.3H2O: C, 53.97; H, 4.94; N, 9.44; S,
3.60. Found: C, 53.37; H, 4.91; N, 9.28; S, 4.21.
