$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1,1-Dimethylethyl
4-[(trans)-bicyclo[3.1.0]hex-3-yl]-3-oxo-1-piperazinecarboxylate. A
mixture of (trans)-bicyclo[3.1.0]hex-3-ylamine hydrochloride (1.10 g,
8.22 mmol), methyl N-{[(1,1-
dimethylethyl)oxy]carbonyl}-N-(2-oxoethyl)glycinate (1.90 g, 8.22 mmol,
see Mendez-Andino, et al, Bioorganic and Medicinal Chemistry, 2007, 15,
2092), DIPEA (1.58 mL, 9.04 mmol), and sodium sulfate (7.00 g, 49.3 mmol)
in MeOH (30 mL) was stirred for 2 hours, then sodium borohydride (0.342
g, 9.04 mmol) was added in portions over 10 minutes. The mixture was
stirred for 2 hours then 60% NaH dispersion in mineral oil (0.624 g,
15.61 mmol) was added in portions over 10 minutes. After 2 hours aqueous
citric acid (30% by wt., 50 mL) was added slowly and the mixture was
filtered through Celite® and the filter pad washed with MeOH. The
filtrate was concentrated at reduced pressure to remove the MeOH and the
remaining aqueous layer was extracted with EtOAc (2x150 mL). The organic
layers were combined, washed with saturated aqueous sodium bicarbonate,
brine, dried over sodium sulfate, filtered and concentrated to dryness at
reduced pressure. The crude product was purified by flash chromatography
(silica gel, EtOAc/hexane). (1.67 g, 73%) as a white solid. 1H NMR (400
MHz, CDCl3): δ 4.68 - 4.82 (m, 1H), 4.05 (s, 2H), 3.57 (t, J = 5.09 Hz,
2H), 3.24 (t, J = 5.08 Hz, 2H), 1.88 (dd, J = 7.70, 12.40 Hz, 2H), 1.69 -
1.80 (m, 2H), 1.46 (s, 9H), 1.23 - 1.33 (m, 2H), 0.29 - 0.43 (m, 2H).
ES-LCMS: m/z 281 (M+1).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM slow addition in stage 4
