$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of (S)-Cyclopropylglycine (3).
Cyclopropyl-Cyclopropylglyoxylic acid 2 potassium salt (50 g, 0.328 mol),
ammonium formate (41.5 g, 0.657 mols) and water (408 mL) were added to a
jacketed 1-L reactor. Magnetic stirring was used to dissolve the solids,
and the temperature was maintained at 40 °C. The solution was adjusted to
pH 8.0 by addition of 4.6 mL of 5 N NaOH. Dithiothreitol (77 mg, 0.5
mmol), NAD (331 mg, 0.5 mmol), formate dehydrogease (814U), and leucine
dehydrogenase (2157 U measured with cyclopropylglyoxylic acid 2 as
substrate) were added. The stirred solution was maintained at 40 °C, and
pH 8.00 was maintained by addition of 5 N NaOH from a pH stat. The
initial concentration of keto acid was 100 mg/mL. After 2 h the
concentration was 67 mg/mL, and after 17 h cyclopropylglyoxylic acid 2
was not detectable. The solution yield was (S)-cyclopropylglycine 3,
usingL-valine as an HPLC standard (correcting for molecular weight).
Yield 37.43 g (99.0%).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM biotransformation, enzymic, stereoselective, recombinant leucine
dehydrogenase from Thermoactinomyces intermedius expressed in Escherichia
coli SC16591 and formate dehydrogenase from Pichia pastoris expressed in
Escherichia coli SC16556 used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Preparation of (S)-1-Cyclopropyl-2-methoxyethanamine by a Chemoenzymatic
Route Using Leucine Dehydrogenase
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Parker, William L.; Hanson, Ronald L.; Goldberg, Steven L.; Tully, Thomas
P.; Goswami, Animesh
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Process Research & Development (2012), 16(3), 464-469

