$DATUM tert-Butyl 4-(pyrimidin-5-ylmethyl)piperazine-1-carboxylate (24f). To a
solution of 1-Boc-piperazine (0.45 g, 2.40 mmol) in anhydrous
dichloromethane (25 mL) was added 5-formylpyrimidine (0.260 g, 2.40 mmol)
followed by sodium triacetoxyborohydride (0.600g, 2.76 mmol) and acetic
acid (0.144 g, 2.40 mmol). The reaction mixture was stirred at room
temperature for 6 h, and then diluted with chloroform (25 mL), washed
with a 10% aqueous NaHCO3 solution (2 x 40 mL), and brine (20 mL). The
organic layer was dried (MgSO4), and concentrated in vacuo. The title
compound was obtained. White solid, yield 0.611 g, 92%. 1H-NMR (500 MHz,
DMSO-d6) 1.38 (s, 9H, CO2(CH3)3), 2.32 (t, J= 5.0 Hz, 4H, piperazine
N-CH), 3.30 (br s, 4H, piperazine N-CH), 3.53 (s, 2H, NCH2-pyrimidine),
8.72 (s, 2H, pyrimidine 4-H and pyrimidine 6-H) 9.09 (s, 1H, pyrimidine
2-H); LC - MS (ESI, m/z): Rt = 1.24 min - 223 (M-tBu)+, 179 (M-BOC)+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Optimization of Imidazo[4,5-b]pyridine-Based Kinase Inhibitors:
Identification of a Dual FLT3/Aurora Kinase Inhibitor as an Orally
Bioavailable Preclinical Development Candidate for the Treatment of Acute
Myeloid Leukemia
