$DATUM tert-Butyl 3-((4-Fluorophenyl)amino)butanoate (5). To a
1,2-dichloroethane solution (146 mL) of 4-fluoroaniline (4.06 g, 36.5
mmol) was added tert-butyl acetoacetate 4 (6.05 mL, 36.5 mmol) and
glacial acetic acid (3.0 mL, 47.5 mmol). Sodium triacetoxyborohydride
(11.6 g, 54.8 mmol) was added in portions, and the reaction was stirred
overnight at room temperature. Saturated aqueous sodium bicarbonate (250
mL) was slowly added, and the two-phase solution was well stirred. The
separated organic portion was washed with saturated aqueous sodium
bicarbonate (1 × 100 mL), water (1 × 100 mL), and brine (1 × 20 mL),
dried over anhydrous magnesium sulfate, filtered, and concentrated. 5
(9.03 g, 98%) as an oil. HPLC: Method 1 = 20% [B], 80% [A] to 70% [B],
30% [A] gradient in 10.0 min, then hold, at 1.5 mL/min, where [A] = 0.1%
trifluoroacetic acid in water, [B] = 0.1% trifluoroacetic acid in
acetonitrile on a Phenomenex Luna C18 (2) 4.6 mm × 3 cm column, 3 µm
packing, 210 nm detection, at 35°C. (2). HPLC: Method 3 = 10% [B], 90%
[A] to 40% [B], 60% [A] gradient in 10.0 min, then hold, at 1.5 mL/min,
where [A] = 0.1% trifluoroacetic acid in water, [B] = 0.1%
trifluoroacetic acid in acetonitrile on a Phenomenex Luna C18 (2) 4.6 mm
× 3 cm column, 3 µm packing, 210 nm detection, at 35°C. 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 6.88 (t, J = 8.8 Hz, 2H), 6.55 (dd, J = 8.8, 4.4 Hz, 2H), 3.80
(sextet, J = 6.4 Hz, 1H), 2.49 (dd, J = 14.8, 5.6 Hz, 1H), 2.33 (dd, J =
14.8, 6.8Hz, 1H), 1.44 (s, 9H), 1.25 (d, J =6.4Hz, 3H).HPLC(method1): t R
= 3.28. LCMS m/z 254.1 (M + H)+. HPLC (method 3): t R = 6.93. LCMS m/z
254.1 (M + H)+.
