$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM The representative procedure for the preparation of
Biaryl-Piperidinyl-Urea compounds 3, 8-20: Procedure for the preparation
of N-[3'-cyano[1,1'-biphenyl]-4-yl]-N-(1-cyclopentyl-
4-piperidinyl)-N'-(3,5-dichlorophenyl)urea (3): To a stirred solution of
4-bromoaniline (10.0 g, 58.13 mmol) and N-Bocpiperidone (11.6 g, 58.13
mmol) was added titanium isopropoxide (20.78 mL, 69.72 mmol) and stirred
at rt for 24 h. The reaction mixture was then cooled to 0 °C and sodium
cyanoborohydride (10.95 g, 174.3 mmol) was added in methanol (30 mL)
dropwise. The reaction was then stirred at 0 °C for 20 mins and at rt for
5 h. The reaction mixture was then diluted with EtOAc:water (3:1),
filtered through Celite. The resulting filtrate was then washed over
brine, dried over Na2SO4, concentrated and chromatographed over silica
gel (eluting EtOAc/hexanes) to yield 20.9 g (49%) of amine 5 as a solid:
1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 7.27 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2 H), 6.50 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2 H),
4.07-4.03 (m, 2 H), 3.58 (br s, 1 H), 3.37 (dddd, J = 12.1, 10.4, 3.9,
3.8 Hz, 1 H), 2.91 (t, J = 12.1 Hz, 2 H), 2.02 (d, J = 12.1 Hz, 2 H),
1.58 (br s, 1 H), 1.47 (s, 9 H), 1.39-1.25 (m, 2 H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Biaryl ureas as potent and orally efficacious melanin concentrating
hormone receptor 1 antagonists for the treatment of obesity
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
