$DATUM 4-Phenoxy-N-(3-pyridylmethyl)aniline A solution of
pyridine-3-carboxaldehyde (2.68 g, 25 mmol) in methanol (75 mL) was
treated with 4-phenoxyaniline (6.11 g, 33 mmol) and refluxed for 1 h. The
solution was cooled on an ice bath and treated in portions with sodium
borohydride (2.50 g, 66 mmol). After the initial effervescence had
subsided, the reaction mixture was allowed to reach room temperature,
stirred 1h, partially concentrated in vacuo to 30mL total volume, and
diluted with water (150 mL). The mixture was stirred for about 1h, during
which time the product had solidified. The precipitate was collected,
washed with water, and air dried. Recrystallization from acetonitrile (2
crops) afforded 5.85g (85%) of 4-phenoxy-N-(3-pyridylmethyl)aniline as a
crystalline white solid. Mp 103-105 °C. 1H NMR (CDCl3): 8.62 (d, 1H, J =
2 Hz); 8.52 (dd, 1H, J = 5 Hz, 2 Hz); 7.69 (d, 1H, J = 8 Hz); 7.25 (m,
3H); 6.99 (t, 1H, J = 8 Hz); 6.89 (m, 4H); 6.61 (m, 2H); 4.33 (s, 2H);
3.98 (br s, 1H). LCMS found 277.3 [M+H]+. Anal. Calcd for C18H16N2O: C,
78.24; H, 5.84; N, 10.14. Found: C, 78.11; H, 5.79; N, 10.16.
