$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM N-cyclopropy4-isopropylaniline To a solution of 4-isopropylaniline (1.35
g, 10 mmol) in MeOH (40 mL) were added
(1-ethoxy-1-trimethylsilyl)cyclopropane (2.1 g, 12 mmol) and AcOH (5 mL)
at room temperature, and the mixture was then stirred at 80 °C for 2.5 h.
To the mixture was added NaB(CN)H3 (1.26 g, 20 mmol) in MeOH (5 mL) at
room temperature, followed by stirring at 80 °C for 3 h. The reaction
mixture was concentrated in vacuo. The residue was suspended in 5% aq.
NaHCO3 and extracted with EtOAc (200 mL). The organic extracts were
successively washed with a 5% aq. NaHCO3 solution, H2O and brine, dried
over Na2SO4, and concentrated in vacuo. The crude product was purified by
silica gel column chromatography to give the title compound. Brown
amorphous solid, yield 1.0 g, 56%. LC-MS (condition C): [M+H]+= 176, t =
3.64 min. 1H NMR(400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.06 (d, J = 8.3 Hz, 2H), 6.74 (d, J
= 8.3 Hz, 2H), 4.07 (brs, 1H), 2.88-2.75 (m, 1H), 2.45-2.38 (m, 1H) 1.21
(d, J = 7.1 Hz, 6H), 0.75-0.66 (m, 2H), 0.53-0.47 (m, 2H).
