$DATUM A mixture of the aniline 21s (1.8 g, 7.47 mmol) and
1-ethoxycyclopropyloxytrimethylsilane (1.6 mL, 8.0 mmol) in AcOH (5 mL)
was stirred at 70 °C for 1 h. After azeotropic distation with toluene to
remove the excess of 1-ethoxycyclopropyloxytrimethylsilane, the residue
was dissolved in MeOH (20 mL). To this solution was added NaBH3CN (540
mg, 8.6 mmol) at room temperature, followed by stirring at 70 °C for 2 h.
After the bulk of the solvent was removed under reduced pressure, the
residue was diluted with EtOAc. The organic layer was washed with aq.
NaOH solution, H2O and brine, dried over Na2SO4, and concentrated in
vacuo. The residue was purified by silica gel column chromatography to
give the title compound 22s. Yield 578 mg, 28%.
N-Cyclopropy2-fluoro-4-isopropy5-(3-methoxypropoxy)aniline (22s). LC-MS
(condition B): [M+H]+= 281, t = 2.42 min. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 6.80
(d, J=12.6 Hz, 1 H), 6.64 (d, J=7.6 Hz, 1 H), 4.23 (br, 1 H), 4.04 (t,
J=6.5 Hz, 2 H), 3.59 (t, J=6.5 Hz, 2 H), 3.37 (s, 3 H), 3.25 - 3.18 (m, 1
H), 2.44 - 2.39 (m, 1 H), 2.09 - 2.03 (m, 2 H), 1.16 (s, 3 H), 1.14 (s, 3
H), 0.74 - 0.71 (m, 2 H), 0.55 - 0.53 (m, 2 H).
