$DATUM H-(t-Bu)Gly-Ala-OEt.TFA (60) (1.5 g, 4.4 mmol, synthesized as described
in General Procedure II) was suspended in MeCN (30 mL). Phthaldialdehyde
(61) (584 mg, 4.4 mol) and acetic acid (25 μL, 0.4 mmol) were added and
the reaction mixture stirred at ambient temperature for 3.5 h. After
concentration in vacuo the crude residue was dissolved in EtOAc (50 mL),
the organic phase washed with 2M HCl (aq) (3 x 20 mL), saturated NaHCO3
(aq) (2 x 20 mL) and brine (20 mL), then dried over MgSO4 and filtered.
The resulting crude material was purified by flash chromatography on
silica, eluting with 0-40 % EtOAc/iso-hexane. Compound 62 as a cream
solid (1.2 g, 0.3 mmol, 78 %). [M + H]+ 347
