$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
1-(1-Methylpiperidin-4-yl)-1,2,3,4-tetrahydroquinoline (58). A solution
of 1,2,3,4-tetrahydroquinoline 54 (1.0 mL, 7.94 mmol) in 20 mL of
1,2-dichloroethane was treated with 1-methylpiperidin-4-one 55 (2.76 mL,
23.8 mmol) followed by sodium triacetoxyborohydride (8.4 g, 39.7 mmol)
and then acetic acid (2.25 mL). The suspension was stirred at room
temperature for 1 day. After this time, the mixture was cooled to 0 °C,
quenched with 5 mL of 1N NaOH, and stirred for 20 min. The suspension was
extracted with 100 mL of CH2Cl2. The organic layer was dried over MgSO4,
filtered, and concentrated to give a light residue which was subjected to
flash chromatography on silica gel using 5% MeOH/CH2Cl2 then 5% 2 M NH3
in MeOH/CH2Cl2. 1-(1-Methylpiperidin-4-yl)-1,2,3,4-tetrahydroquinoline, a
yellow oil was obtained (440 mg, 24.1%). 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ: 7.07-7.02 (m,
1H), 6.95 (d, J = 7.5 Hz, 1H), 6.65 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H), 6.55 (pseudo t,
J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 3.65-3.55 (m, 1H), 3.20 (t, J = 5.7 Hz, 2H), 2.99-2.95
(m, 2H), 2.73 (t, J = 6.0 Hz, 2H), 2.31 (s, 3H), 2.11-2.05 (m, 2H),
1.93-1.73 (m, 6H). MS (ESI): 231.2 (M + 1, 100%).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Design, Synthesis, and Biological Evaluation of
3,4-Dihydroquinolin-2(1H)-one and 1,2,3,4-Tetrahydroquinoline-Based
Selective Human Neuronal Nitric Oxide Synthase (nNOS) Inhibitors
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
