$DATUM N-(4-Chlorobenzyl)-1-(5-nitrothiophen-2-yl)methanamine (27).
5-Nitrothiophene-2-carboxaldehyde (0.57 g, 3.6 mmol) was added to a
solution of 4-chlorobenzylamine (0.44 mL, 3.6 mmol) in DCE (12.0 mL) at
room temperature. After the mixture was stirred for 5 min, acetic acid
(0.22 mL, 3.6 mmol) and sodium triacetoxyborohydride (1.10 g, 5.0 mmol)
were added at room temperature. After being stirred for 16 h at room
temperature, the mixture was quenched with saturated aqueous NaHCO3
solution. The organic phase was dried over sodium sulfate, and the
solvent was evaporated in vacuo. The residue was purified over silica gel
(20−60% EtOAc in petroleum ether) to give the title compound. Pale yellow
oil (0.55 g, 1.9 mmol, 54%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.77 (d, J = 4.2
Hz, 1H), 7.32−7.26 (m, 4H), 6.86 (dt, J = 4.2, 1.0 Hz, 1H), 3.98 (d, J =
1.0 Hz, 2H), 3.82 (brs, 2H). MS m/z = 283.0 (M + H)+. HRMS calcd for
C12H11O2N2ClS requires m/z 283.0303, found 283.0306.
