$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of
[6-Benzhydryl-1-(4-fluorobenzyl)piperidin-3-yl](4-fluorobenzyl)amine
(17).:
cis-(6-Benzhydryl-1-methylpiperidin-3-yl)(4-fluorobenzyl)methylamine (15)
(0.07 g, 0.18 mmol) were reacted with 4-fluorobenzaldehyde (0.022 g, 0.17
mmol), acetic acid (0.01 g, 0.18 mmol), and NaBH3CN(0.01 g, 0.22 mmol) in
CH2ClCH2Cl to give a crude product which was purified by flash
chromatography (EtOAc/hexane = 3/2) to produce 17, as a white solid,
yield 0.07 g, (76%). mp: 138-139 °C. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ 1.46 (1H,
d, J =12.8 Hz, H-5ax), 1.56-1.62(1H, m, H-5eq), 1.75-1,83 (2H, m, H-4),
2.60 (1H, d, J = 11.2 Hz, H-2ax), 2.72-2.83 (2H, m, H-3eq, H-2eq), 3.50
(1H, dd, J = 11.2 Hz, J = 2.4 Hz, H-6ax), 3.72-3.84 (4H, m, CH2C6H4F),
4.49 (1H, d, J = 11.2 Hz, CH(Ph)2), 6.80-6.88(2H, m, ArH, ortho F),
6.99(2H, t, J = 8.5 Hz, ArH,ortho F), 7.13-7.29 (14H, m, ArH). mp:
177-180 °C. Anal. [C32H32- FN2•2HCl•2.6H2O] C, H, N.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Further Structurally Constrained Analogues of
cis-(6-Benzhydrylpiperidin-3-yl)benzylamine with Elucidation of Bioactive
Conformation : Discovery of 1,4-Diazabicyclo[3.3.1]nonane Derivatives and
Evaluation of Their Biological Properties for the Monoamine Transporters
