$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
6-Benzyloxymethyl-5-[4-(4-chloro-benzylamino)-phenyl]-pyrimidine-2,4-diamine.
To a solution of pyrimidine-2,4-diamine (1.62 g, 5.05 mmol) in 1 M
NaOAc/HOAc in MeOH (80 mL, pH 4) was added 4-chlorobenzaldehyde (851 mg,
6.06 mmol). The resulting mixture was stirred for 15 min followed by slow
addition of NaBH3CN (375 mg, 6.06 mmol). The reaction mixture was stirred
for 16 h at 25 °C. The product was diluted with EtOAc (80 mL) and washed
with 1.2 M HCl (75 mL), 2 M NaOH (2 x 100 mL), and brine (100 mL). The
crude material was purified by silica gel chromatography (EtOAc to 10%
MeOH in EtOAc
gradient).6-Benzyloxymethyl-5-[4-(4-chloro-benzylamino)-phenyl]-pyrimidine-2,4-diamine,
yield 1.56 g, 70%.
5-[4-(4-Chloro-benzylamino)-phenyl]-6-phenethyl-pyrimidine-2,4-diamine,
yield 49%. 1H NMR (300 MHz,DMSO-d6) δ 7.31-7.43 (m, 4H), 7.10-7.21 (m,
3H), 6.91-6.93(d, J = 6.4 Hz, 2H), 6.77 (d, J = 8.5 Hz, 2H), 6.59 (d, J =
8.5 Hz,2H), 6.35 (t, J = 5.8 Hz, 1H), 5.86 (s, 2H), 5.39 (s, 2H), 4.27
(d,J = 5.8 Hz, 2H), 2.69-2.74 (m, 2H), 2.33-2.39 (m, 2H). MS (ESI)m/z )
430 [M + H]+, 428 [M - H]-. Anal. (C25H24ClN5) C, H,N.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM 2,4-Diaminopyrimidine Derivatives as Potent Growth Hormone Secretagogue
