$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Step 2: A mixture of N-(phenylmethyl)-1-propanamine (1.60 g, 10.7 mmol),
4-nitrobenzaldehyde (1.62 g, 10.7 mmol) and sodium triacetoxyborohydride
(4.54 g, 21.4 mmol) in 1,2-dichloroethane (50 mL) was stirred at RT
overnight. Sat. NaHCO3 solution (25 mL) was added and the mixture was
stirred for 20 minutes. The phases were separated and the aqueous phase
was washed with DCM. The combined organics were washed with brine, dried
over Na2SO4 and concentrated in vacuo. The crude product was purified on
reversed phase chromatography eluting with acetonitrile and water to
afford N-[(4-nitrophenyl)methyl]-N-(phenylmethyl)-1-propanamine. 2.03 g,
7.13 mmol, 66.6 % yield. 1H-NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ ppm 8.15 (d, J = 8.8
Hz, 2H), 7.53 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2H), 7.29-7.38 (m, 4H), 7.22-7.27 (m, 1H),
3.62 (s, 2H), 3.58 (s, 2H), 2.34-2.44 (m, 2H), 1.48-1.60 (m, 2H), 0.86
(t, J = 7.3 Hz, 3H). LCMS: rt = 2.202 minutes, MH+ = 285.1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
