$DATUM 1-((2-chloro-4-morpholinothieno[3,2-d]pyrimidin-6-yl)methyl)-N,N-dimethylpiperidin-4-amine
(35) To a solution of 4-(dimethylamino)piperidine (2.00 g, 15.6 mmol) in
1,2-dichloroethane (123 mL) was added , acetic acid (0.739 mL, 13.0
mmol), 2-chloro-4-morpholinothieno[3,2-d]pyrimidine-6-carbaldehyde (31)
(3.69 g, 13.0 mmol) and sodium triacetoxyborohydride (3.58 g, 16.9 mmol).
The reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature for 16 h. LC-MS of
the reaction mixture showed the desired product. The reaction mixture was
quenched with 2M HCl and partitioned between dichloromethane. The acidic
aqueous layer was extracted twice to remove impurities and SM. The aqeous
layer was basified to pH11 with sat sodium carbonate and extracted with
DCM. The organic layer was washed with brine, dried over Na2SO4, filtered
and concentrated to yield
1-((2-chloro-4-morpholinothieno[3,2-d]pyrimidin-6-yl)methyl)-N,N-dimethylpiperidin-4-amine
35. Off white powder, yield 4.50 g, 87%. LCMS m/z [M+H]+ 397.2. 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.14 (s, 1H), 4.05 - 3.95 (m, 4H), 3.88 - 3.80 (m,
4H), 3.77 (s, 2H), 3.03-2.94 (m, 2H), 2.30 (s, 6H), 2.19-2.05 (m, 3H),
1.87-1.77 (m, 3H), 1.57 (qd, J= 12.1, 3.7 Hz, 2H).
