$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of Compound S2. To a solution of S1 (4.3 g, 0.020 mol) and
hydroxylamine hydrochloride (2.78 g, 0.040 mol) in ethanol (60 mL) was
added NaOH (1.6 g, 0.040 mol) and H2O (15 mL) solution dropwise over 15
minutes, and the reaction was stirred at reflux for 20 h. The mixture was
filtered through Celite, and the solvent was removed in vacuo. The
mixture was extracted with dichloromethane (x4), and dried over anhydrous
sodium sulfate, filtered, and the solvent was removed in vacuo. Sodium
(5.83 g) was added to toluene (72 mL) at room temperature, and the
mixture was heated to 100 °C. To the solution was added dropwise a
solution of the above residue in toluene (50 mL) and 1-propanol (30 mL),
and the reaction was stirred at reflux for 12 h. After cooling to 80 °C,
2-propanol was added to the reaction solution, and the solution was
cooled to ambient temperature. The solution was diluted with water (160
mL) and acidified to pH 1 with concentrated hydrogen chloride solution,
and the mixture was extracted with ethyl acetate. The aqueous layer was
basified to pH 12 with sodium hydroxide solution, and the mixture was
extracted with ethyl acetate, dried over anhydrous sodium sulfate,
filtered, and the solvent was removed in vacuo. To a solution of the
residue in THF (50 mL) was added Boc2O (4.8 g, 0.022 mol), and the
reaction was stirred at room temperature for 3 days. After concentration
under reduced pressure, the residue was triturated with diethylether, and
filtered to afford the title compound. The solvent of the filtrate was
removed in vacuo, and the residue was purified by column chromatography
on silica gel. The solvent was removed in vacuo, the residue was
triturated with diethylether, and filtered to afford compound S2. White
crystal, yield 50%. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 500 MHz) δ 1.43 (9H, s), 1.48 (2H, m),
1.68 (2H, m), 1.81 (2H, m), 2.01 (2H, m), 3.20 (2H, m), 3.53 (2H, s),
3.81 (1H, m), 4.33 (1H, d, J = 8.6 Hz), 7.22- 7.37 (5H, m); 13C NMR
(CDCl3, 126 MHz) δ 26.5, 28.4, 38.7, 42.8, 56.1, 58.7, 79.2, 126.7,
128.2, 128.5, 140.0, 155.3.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Preparation and activities of macromolecule conjugates of the CCR5
antagonist Maraviroc
