$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Step 6.
5-(3-(2-(2,2-Dimethyl-1,3-dioxan-5-yl)-1,2,3,4-tetrahydroisoquinolin-6-yl)-1,2,4-oxadiazol-5-yl)-2-isopropoxybenzonitrile
(62). A stirred suspension of compound 61 (0.252 g, 0.531 mmol) in
dichloromethane (DCM) (8 mL) under nitrogen was treated with
2,2-dimethyl-1,3-dioxan-5-one (0.19 mL, 1.59 mmol) followed by sodium
triacetoxyborohydride (0.51 g, 2.39 mmol). The resulting mixture was
stirred under nitrogen at room temperature for 19 h then was treated with
a saturated NaHCO3 aqueous solution (5 mL). The biphasic mixture was
vigorously stirred for 15 min then the layers were separated. The aqueous
phase was extracted with DCM (3×5 mL) and the combined organic phases
were dried by filtering through a cartridge fitted with a hydrophobic
frit, and the solvent was evaporated under a stream of nitrogen to give
the title compound (233 mg, 0.5 mmol, 92%) as a cream solid which was
used in the subsequent reaction without further purification. LCMS
(method high pH): Retention time 0.99 min, [M+H]+ = 475.29.
