$DATUM To a solution of
(3S*,4S*,5R*)-3-((1H-indazol-5-yl)methyl)-5-((3-(tert-butyl)benzyl)amino)-4-
hydroxytetrahydro-2H-thiopyran 1,1-dioxide hydrochloride (0.105 g, 0.27
mmol) in MeOH-CH2Cl2 1:1 (2 mL) was added NaOAc (0.071 g, 0.85 mmol) and
3-tert-butyl-benzaldehyde (0.05 g, 0.29 mmol) dissolved in CH2Cl2 (2 mL).
The reaction mixture was stirred at 25 °C for 2 h before NaBH3CN (0.026
g, 0.4 mmol) was added followed by stirring for 2 h. The reaction mixture
was acidified with 1N HCl, stirred for 15 min, basified with aq. K2CO3
and extracted with EtOAc. The combined organic layers were washed with
brine, dried over MgSO4, filtered through a plug of silica gel and
concentrated to provide after crystallization from diisopropylether.
0.102 g (86%) of (3S*,4S*,5R*)-3-((1H-indazol-5-
yl)methyl)-5-((3-(tert-butyl)benzyl)amino)-4-hydroxytetrahydro-2H-thiopyran
1,1-dioxide. 1H NMR (600 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 13.02 (s, 1H), 7.98 (s, 1H),
7.54 (s, 1H), 7.48 (d, J = 8.7 Hz, 1H), 7.38 (s, 1H), 7.05-7.30 (m, 4H),
5.33 (br s, 1H), 3.83 (d, J = 13.2 Hz, 1H), 3.66-3.80 (m, 2H), 2.75-3.45
(m, 7H), 2.61 (dd, J = 13.7, 10.6 Hz, 1H), 2.12 (m, 1H), 1.32 (s, 9H);
LC/MS (ESI, positive ion): m/z 442 (M+H); HRMS m/z 442.21599 [(M+H) +
calcd for C24H32N3O3S + , 442.21589].
