$DATUM (3R,4S,5S)-3-((3-(tert-Butyl)benzyl)amino)-5-(3-fluoro-4-nitrobenzyl)-4-hydroxytetrahydro-2H-thiopyran
1,1-dioxide (13): To a solution of
(3R,4S,5S)-3-amino-5-(3-fluoro-4-nitrobenzyl)-4-hydroxy-
tetrahydro-2H-thiopyran 1,1-dioxide hydrochloride (2.8 g, 7.8 mmol) in
MeOH-CH2Cl2 1:1 (60 mL) was added NaOAc (1.3 g, 15.6 mmol) and
3-tert-butyl-benzaldehyde (1.4 g, 8.6 mmol) dissolved in CH2Cl2 (60 mL).
The reaction mixture was stirred at 25 °C for 0.5 h before NaBH3CN (0.78
g, 11.8 mmol) was added followed by stirring for 2 h. The reaction
mixture was acidified with 1N HCl, stirred for 15 min, basified with
K2CO3 solution and extracted with EtOAc. The combined organic layers were
washed with brine, dried over MgSO4 and concentrated. Flash column
chromatography (hexane- CH2Cl2-MeOH 20:20:1 to 1:20:5). 2.9 g (80%) of
(3R,4S,5S)-3-((3-(tert-butyl)benzyl)amino)-
5-(3-fluoro-4-nitrobenzyl)-4-hydroxytetrahydro-2H-thiopyran 1,1-dioxide
as a light yellow foam. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.02 (t, J = 8.0 Hz,
1H), 7.27-7.38 (m, 3H), 7.07-7.21 (m, 3H), 4.14 (br s, 1H), 3.90 (d, J =
12.9 Hz, 1H), 3.72-3.82 (m, 1H), 3.64 (m, 1H), 3.41 (dt, J = 13.3, 4.3
Hz, 1H), 3.25 (dd, J = 13.7, 3.2 Hz, 1H), 3.12 (m, 1H), 3.01 (t, J = 10.0
Hz, 1H), 2.78-2.92 (m, 2H), 2.70 (q, J = 13.3 Hz, 2H), 2.24 (m, 1H), 1.33
(m, 9H); LC/MS (ESI, positive ion): m/z 465 (M+H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of Cyclic Sulfone Hydroxyethylamines as Potent and Selective
