$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Chemistry. General Procedure for Reductive
Amination (Method A). A solution of the corresponding spiropiperidine
derivative and the appropriate aldehyde was stirred at room temperature
in the appropriate solvent (0.15−0.55 M tetrahydrofuran or
1,2-dichloroethane) for 10−60 min (t1). Then sodium triacetoxyborohydride
(1.2−2.0 equiv) was added and the reaction mixture was stirred at room
temperature until it was completed (2−16 h, t2). The reaction mixture was
treated with ice/saturated solution of sodium bicarbonate, and the
organic phase was extracted with ethyl acetate, dichloromethane, or
tert-butyl ethyl ether (S2). The organic layer was separated, washed with
brine, dried over magnesium sulfate, filtered, and concentrated under
vacuum. The resulting crude product was purified by chromatography.
2-Chloro-4,4-difluoro-1'-[(3-methy1H-pyrazo4-yl)methyl]-spiro[5H-thieno[2,3-c]pyran-7,4'-piperidine]
(33). The title compound was essentially prepared following general
method A using 25 (105 g, 375 mmol), 3-methy1H-pyrazole-4-carbaldehyde
(43.40 g, 394.12 mmol), and sodium triacetoxyborohydride (95.46 g, 450.42
mmol) using 1.58 L of tetrahydrofuran (t1 = 60 min, t2 = 15 h, S = ethyl
acetate). A 140 g amount of the title compound was obtained (100% yield).
LC-MS (ESI) m/z: 374 (M + H)+. tR = 2.09 min, method 2. 1H NMR (300 MHz,
CDCl3) δ: 7.50 (s, 1H), 6.95 (s, 1H), 4.03 (t, J = 10.3 Hz, 2H), 3.47 (s,
2H), 2.86−2.78 (m, 2H), 2.40 (t, J = 11.4 Hz, 2H), 2.30 (s, 3H),
2.11−2.04 (m, 2H), 1.96−1.84 (m, 2H). HRMS (ESI): calcd for
C16H18ClF2N3OS 373.0827, found 373.0834.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of a Novel Series of Orally Active Nociceptin/Orphanin FQ (NOP)
Receptor Antagonists Based on a
Dihydrospiro(piperidine-4,7'-thieno[2,3-c]pyran) Scaffold
