$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM cis-3-Bis(phenylmethyl)aminocyclobutanemethyl Benzoate Hydrochloride .
Charge a 500-mL,4-necked,round bottomed flask with 24.8 g (0.121 mol) of
cyclobutanone,22.5 g (0.115mol) of dibenzyle amine,and 101.5 g (112.5 mL)
of ethyl acetate. Stir the homogeneous reaction mixture for AEW541 h at
20-25 °C. Charge a 2-L, 4-necked, round-bottomed flask with 34.1 g (0.161
mol) of sodium triacetoxyborohydride and 203.0 g (225 mL) of ethyl
acetate. Stir for 15 min at room temperature. Add the (
cyclobutanone+dibenzyle amine) solution over 30-40 min. Stir the
heterogeneous reaction mixture at 20-25°C for 16 h. Add 426.4 g (410 mL)
of 2N NaOH over 15 min. Stir for 1 h at 20-25 °C. Caution: H2 evolution.
Remove the lower aqueous layer and wash the ethylacetate solution of
ester with 2 x 300 g of water. Mark a 1-L round bottomed flask at 130 mL.
Charge the flask with the ethylacetate solution of ester and concentrate
to a volume of 130-150 mL, using atmospheric distillation conditions.
Cool the residual solution to 65 °C and add 94.2 g (120 mL) of
2-propanol. Hold the solution at 65-70 °C. Add 12.0 g (0.121 mol) of
hydrochloricacid (37 wt %) over 5-10 min. Cool from 65 °C to 43-45 °C. At
45 °C seed the reaction mixture with 20 mg of ester.Cool from 43-45 °C to
32-33 °C over 0.5 h. Stir at 32-33°C for at least 90 min. Cool to 20-25
°C over 0.5 h. Hold 1 h at 20-25 °C. Isolate the solid by filtration and
wash the cake with 78.5 g (100 mL) of 2-propanol. Dry the cake on the
funnel for 30 min, then dry in a vacuum oven at 60-65 °C (35-50 mm Hg)
for at least 16 h, to yield ester 29.9 g (62% yield), 98.9% cis isomer;
1.1% trans isomer by HPLC analysis; white solid ,mp 165 °C; 1H NMR
(CDCl3) δ 8.0 (d, j) 9.0 Hz, 2H), 7.55 (m, 13H), 4.35 (d, j ) 9.0 Hz,
2H), 4.07 (m, 4H), 3.31 (m,1H), 2.86 (m, 2H), 2.20 (m, 3H); 13C NMR
(DMSO, d6) δ165.61, 133.31, 131.43, 130.17, 129.92, 129.51, 129.28,
129.24, 128.70, 128.63, 128.52, 67.49, 551.6, 54.38, 29.70, 26.40; MS m/
z 386 (M+). Anal. Calcd for C26H28ClNO2: C, 74.00; H, 6.69; N, 3.32; Cl,
8.40. Found: C, 74.08; H, 6.65; N, 3.31; Cl,8.62
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective (in stage 2), cis:trans=98.9:1.1, optimization study,
optimized on reaction conditions, alternatively MeCN and toluene used as
solvent, scalable
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A concise synthesis of a novel insulin-like growth factor I receptor
(IGF-IR) inhibitor
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
