$DATUM 1-(2,6-difluorobenzyl)-3-(2-(N-methyl-N-(2-(2-pyridy)ethy)-aminoethyl)-5-bromo-6-methyl-uracil
(10) To a mixture of the aldehyde 7 (6.71g, 18.0 mmol) and
N-methyl-2-(2-pyridyl)ethylamine (2.5 g, 18.3 mmol) in 1,2-dichloroethane
(100 ml), NaBH(OAc)3 (7.6 mg, 2.0 eq.) was added in 4 portions within 10
minutes. The mixture was stirred at r.t. for 2 hours and then diluted
with water (100ml) and chloroform (200ml) with stirring for 5 minutes.
The organic layer was separated, dired over Na2SO4, concentrated to yield
a brown oil, which was purified by silica gel chromatography using
CHCl3/MeOH system to yield the desired product 10 (6.5g, 73%).
1-(2,6-difluorobenzyl)-3-(2-(N-methyl-N-(2-(2-pyridy)ethy)-aminoethyl)-5-bromo-6-methyl-uracil
(10), yield (6.5g, 73%). MS (M+H): 493.1/495.1; 1H NMR (CDCl3), δ, 8.50
(1H, d, J = 4.5 Hz), 7.58(1H, dt, J = 7.5, 1.8 Hz), 7.31-7.25 (1H, m),
7.20(1H, d, J = 7.5 Hz), 7.13-7.06 (1H, m), 6.69-6.87(2H, m), 5.32 (2H,
s), 4.14 (2H, t, J = 7.5 Hz), 2.95-2.78 (4H, m), 2.70 (2H, t, J =7.5 Hz),
2.50 (3H, s), 2.39(3H, s).
