$DATUM Synthesis of N-[2-(N-Boc-L-phenylalanyloxy)ethyl]glycine allyl esters
(7). Glycine allyl ester trifluoroacetate 6 (2.8 g, 12.2 mmol) was
dissolved in methanol, then DIPEA (2 mL, 11.48 mmol) and the aldehyde 3
(9.1 mmol) were added under magnetic stirring, followed by addition of
acetic acid (10.5 mmol) and, slowly portion-wise, NaBH3CN (0.61 g, 9.7
mmol). After 30 min the reaction mixture was evaporated and the residue
was dissolved in ethyl acetate. The organic layer was washed with a
saturated aqueous solution of NaHCO3 and then with a saturated aqueous
solution of KHSO4, dried over anhydrous sodium sulphate and evaporated
under vacuum. The crude product was purified by flash-chromatography
(SiO2) with ethyl acetate-hexane (v/v = 1:1). The purified product was
under the form of colorless oil. 7 as colorless oil, yield 46%. 1H-NMR
(300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.35 (s, 9H), 1.80 (br s, 1H), 2.75-2.77 (m, 2H), 3.05
(d, 2H, J = 8,6 Hz), 3.35 (s, 2H), 4.15-4.17 (m, 2H), 4.55-4.60 (m, 3 H),
5.00 (br d, 1H), 5.14-5.17 (m, 1H), 5.21-5.28 (m, 1H), 5.80-5.95 (m, 1H),
7.05-7.30 (m, 5H); 13C-NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 171.89, 171.81, 155.05,
136.07, 131.84, 129.32, 128.49, 127.00, 118.74, 79.90, 65.43, 64.76,
54.52, 50.53, 47.56, 38.48, 28.28; FAB-MS: m/z = 407.14 [MH]+. Calculated
for [C21H31N2O6]+: 407.22.
