$DATUM 2-(1-((2-chloro-4-morpholinothieno[3,2-d]pyrimidin-6-yl)methyl)piperidin-4-yl)propan-2-ol
(36). To a solution of 2-(4-piperidyl)-2-propanol (0.166 g, 1.16 mmol) in
1,2-dichloroethane (2.8 mL) was added acetic acid (0.055 mL, 0.97 mmol),
2-chloro-4-morpholinothieno[3,2-d]pyrimidine-6- carbaldehyde (31) (0.275
g, 0.969 mmol and sodium triacetoxyborohydride (0.267 g, 1.26 mmol). The
reaction was stirred at room temperature for 16 h prior to partitioning
between DCM and saturated sodium bicarbonate. The organic layer was
washed with brine, dried over anhydrous sodium sulfate, filtered and
concentrated. The crude product was purified by flash chromatography
(0-15% MeOH gradient in DCM) to give
2-(1-((2-chloro-4-morpholinothieno[3,2-d]pyrimidin-6-yl)methyl)piperidin-4-
yl)propan-2-ol 36. Yield 0.378 g, 95%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of Novel PI3-Kinase δ Specific Inhibitors for the Treatment of
Rheumatoid Arthritis: Taming CYP3A4 Time-Dependent Inhibition
