$DATUM Step 2: A mixture of N-{[4-(trifluoromethyl)phenyl]methyl}-1-propanamine
(2.00 g, 9.21 mmol), 4-nitrobenzaldehyde (1.39 g, 9.21 mmol) and sodium
triacetoxyborohydride (3.90 g, 18.41 mmol) in 1,2-dichloroethane (50 mL)
was stirred at RT overnight. LCMS showed some SM remained. More
4-nitrobenzaldehyde (0.85 g) and sodium triacetoxyborohydride (1.6 g)
were added. After 5 hours, LCMS showed the reaction finished. Sat NaHCO3
solution (25 mL) was added. The mixture was stirred for 20 minutes. The
phases were separated and the aqueous phase was washed with DCM for 3
times. The combined organics were washed with brine, dried over Na2SO4
and concentrated. The crude product
N-[(4-nitrophenyl)methyl]-N-{[4-(trifluoromethyl)phenyl]methyl}-1-propanamine
was used directly in the next step. 4.1 g, 7.91 mmol, 68% purity, 86%
yield. LCMS: rt = 2.678 minutes, MH+ = 353.1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM incremental addition of4-nitrobenzaldehyde and sodium
triacetoxyborohydride (stage 1)
