$DATUM Synthesis of MMPI precursor 23. (R)-tert-Butyl
2-((4-(2-(2-(2-(2-azidoethoxy)ethoxy)ethoxy)ethoxy)benzyl)amino)-3-methylbutanoate
(18). D-Valin-tert-butylester hydrochloride (8.16 g, 38.93 mmol, 1.05
eq.) and 4-(2-(2-(2-(2-azidoethoxy)ethoxy)ethoxy)ethoxy)benzaldehyde (17,
11.99 g, 37.08 mmol), prepared following literature procedure, were
dissolved in dichloroethane (13 mL) under argon atmosphere. Triethylamine
(7.7 mL, 55.62 mmol, 1.50 eq.), molecular sieve and sodium triacetoxy
borohydride (NaBH(OAc)3, 95%, 11.71 g, 51.91 mmol, 1.4 eq.) were added
and the reaction mixture was stirred under argon atmosphere at room
temperature. After 24 h again NaBH(OAc)3 (5.00 g, 22.16 mmol) was added
and the mixture was stirred for another 18 hours. Quenching with
saturated aqueous NaHCO3 (200 mL), extraction with ethyl acetate (3 × 100
mL), drying over magnesium sulfate and concentration under reduced
pressure yielded the crude product, which was purified by column
chromatography (silica gel, CH/EA, 2:1). The product was isolated.
Compound: 18. Yield: (16.00 g, 33.37 mmol, 90%). Colorless oil. 1H NMR
(300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.24 (d, ArH, 3JH,H = 8.7 Hz, 2H), 6.86 (d, ArH, 3JH,H
= 8.7 Hz, 2H), 4.15-4.09 (m, CH2CH2O, 2H), 3.89-3.82 (m, CH2CH2O, 2H),
3.76 (AB, d, NHCH2, 2JH,H = 11.4 Hz, 1H), 3.76-3.63 (m, CH2CH2O, 10H),
3.51 (AB, d, NHCH2, 2JH,H = 12.7 Hz, 1H), 3.38 (t, CH2N3, 3JH,H = 5.0 Hz,
