$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM [4-(4-butyry5-methypyrazo1-yl)-phenyl]-5-chloro-1-[2-(8-methy9-oxo-octahydropyrazino[1,2-a]pyrazin-2-yl)-2-oxoethyl]-1H-indole-3-carboxamide
(102). To a mixture of 50h (3.20 g, 6.68 mmol) and
piperazine-2-carboxylic acid methyl ester (1.01 g, 7.01 mmol) in solution
in DCM (33 mL) were successively added Et3N (2.82 mL, 20.04 mmol), and
BOP-Cl (2.55 g, 10.02 mmol). The reaction mixture was stirred for 48 h
and evaporated to dryness. The solide residue was then suspended in EtOAc
and the organic phase was washed with water, with brine, dried on Na2SO4,
evaporated and dried under vacuum to produce 3.60 g of a white powder.
The product obtained (3.60 g, 5.92 mmol) was then re-suspended in MeOH
(68 mL) and tert-butyl methyl(2-oxoethyl)carbamate (1.05 g, 5.92 mmol),
sodium cyanoborohydride (0.374 g, 5.92 mmol) and AcOH (2 mL) were
successively added. After stirring at RT for 20 h, the reaction mixture
was evaporated to dryness and then the raw reaction product was purified
by silica gel chromatography, eluting with DCM/MeOH mixture (gradient
from 0 to 5% of MeOH). The powder obtained was dissolved in TFA (9 mL)
and stirred at RT for 4 h. The reaction mixture was poured into an aq. 2N
NaOH solution (137 mL). The heterogeneous medium was stirred for 15 min
and then extracted with EtOAc. The organic phase was washed with water,
with brine and then evaporated to dryness. The solid residue was purified
by silica gel column chromatography, eluting with DCM/MeOH mixture
(gradient from 2 to 10% of MeOH). The product was triturated with
isopropylether and then filtered, obtaining 102. White powder, yield 2.19
g, 57%. 1H NMR: DMSO-d6 (500 MHz): δ (ppm): 8.29 (br, 1H), 8.23 (s, 1H),
8.22 (d, J = 2.2 Hz, 1H), 7.96 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2H), 7.56 (d, J = 7.8 Hz,
1H), 7.49 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2H), 7.26 (br, 1H), 5.61 - 5.26 (m, 2H), 4.87 -
4.29 (m, 1H), 4.22 (d, J = 13.0 Hz, 1H), 4.05 (d, J = 9.0 Hz, 1H), 3.83 -
3.65 (m, 3H), 3.63 - 3.42 (m, 3H), 3.37 - 3.04 (m, 2H), 2.99 - 2.85 (m,
3H), 2.81 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H), 2.52 (s, 3H), 1.63 (sext, J = 7.3 Hz, 2H),
0.93 (t, J = 7.3 Hz, 3H). LCMS (method A): MH+ (tR) = 630 (7.96 min). C
60.85%, H 5.82%, N 14.92%, C33H36ClN7O4.H2O. m.p. = 220 °C.
