$DATUM Step 4 A solution of 13 (0.7 g, 3.5 mmol),
N-(2-aminoethyl)-3-(S)-hydroxy-pyrrolidine18 (1.36 g, 10.5 mmol) and
sodium triacetoxyborohydride (2.2 g, 10.5 mmol) were refluxed in CH2Cl2
(50 mL). After 24 h, the organic layer was washed with water (3x), dried
over sodium sulfate and concentrated in vacuo. The crude reaction mixture
(60mg) and 3-chloro-4-(trifluoromethyl)phenyl isocyanate (50 mg, 0.29
mmol) were stirred in CH2Cl2 (5 mL). After 24 h, the reaction solution
was loaded directly onto a preparative TLC plate and purified (15%
EtOAc/Hex) to provide 16 (35.9 mg, 36%). and 17 (38.6 mg, 39%). 16: 1H
NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 10.72 (s, 1H), 7.57-7.71 (m, 4H), 7.42-7.53 (m,
2H), 7.03 (t, J = 9.8 Hz, 1H), 4.48 (m, 1H), 4.29 (t, J = 12.0, 4.0 Hz,
1H), 3.00-3.17 (m, 4H), 2.66-2.85 (m, 4H), 1.76-2.52 (m, 8H), 1.60-1.70
(m, 2H), 1.30-1.45 (m, 2H). LCMS: 519.1, rt. = 5.46 min (M+H+), 98%
purity; HRMS (FAB) m/z 519.2392 [(M+H)+; calcd for C27H30F4N4O2:
519.2305] 17: 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 10.73 (s, 1H), 7.67-7.73 (m, 2H),
7.36-7.51 (m, 4H), 7.03 (t, J = 9.8 Hz, 1H), 4.51 (m, 1H), 4.24 (t, J =
12.0, 4.0 Hz, 1H), 3.35 (t, J = 4.0 Hz, 2H), 3.10 (m, 1H), 2.75-2.90 (m,
4H), 2.52 (m, 2H), 2.22 (m, 1H), 1.80-2.00 (m, 6H), 1.45-1.70 (m, 4H).
LCMS: 519.1, rt. = 5.46 min (M+H+), 98% purity; HRMS (FAB) m/z 519.2387
[(M+H)+; calcd for C27H30F4N4O2: 519.2305].
