$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: METHOD 19. tert-Butyl
N-[3-[1-[4-oxo-3-(1,3-thiazol-4-ylmethyl)thieno[3,2-d]pyrimidin-2-yl]propylamino]propyl]carbamate.
2-(1-Aminopropyl)-3-(1,3-thiazol-4-ylmethyl)thieno[2,3-e]pyrimidin-4-one
(method 17) (0.20 g, 0.58 mmol), Et3N (90 μL, 0.64 mmol) in
dichloroethane (5.8 mL) at 25°C was treated with tert-butyl
N-(3-oxopropyl)carbamate (0.092 g, 0.52 mmol). The reaction mixture was
stirred at r.t. for 30 min and then Na(OAc)3BH (0.124 g, 0.58 mmol) was
added. The reaction mixture was further stirred at r.t. for 1 h. and
subsequently quenched with satd NaHCO3 (10 mL) and further diluted with
DCM (10 mL). The organic layer was dried with Na2SO4. The solvents were
removed under vacuum to give a residue that was purified by silica column
chromatography (4 : 1 EtOAc : dichloroethane-8 : 1 EtOAc :
dichloroethane). tert-Butyl
N-[3-[1-[4-oxo-3-(1,3-thiazol-4-ylmethyl)thieno[3,2-d]pyrimidin-2-yl]propylamino]propyl]carbamate
(0.040 g, 15%). m/z 464 (MH+).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of
(+)-N-(3-Aminopropyl)-N-[1-(5-benzyl-3-methyl-4-oxo-[1,2]thiazolo[5,4-d]pyrimidin-6-yl)-2-methylpropyl]-4-methylbenzamide
(AZD4877), a Kinesin Spindle Protein Inhibitor and Potential Anticancer
Agent
