$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of (S)-1-(5-Fluoropyrimidin-2-yl)-ethylamine Hydrochloride
Using Commercial V. fluvialis. (S)-α-Methylbenzylamine (68.0 mL, 0.53
mol) was added to a solution of monobasic potassium phosphate (13.21 g,
0.097 mol) in water (1020 mL). The pH of the solution was adjusted to pH
7.5 by the addition of acetic acid (26.0 mL, 0.45 mol). Pyridoxal
phosphate (0.643 g, 0.0024 mol) was added, followed by
2-acetyl-5-fluoropyrimidine (68.0 g, 0.49 mol), a buffered solution of V.
fluvialis transaminase enzyme (182 mL, 35.3 kU) and toluene (340 mL). The
reaction mixture was adjusted to pH 7.5 with potassium carbonate (6.71 g,
0.053 mol) and then held at 29 °C for 18 h with stirring. Harborlite
(12.0 g) was added and the reaction mixture was stirred for a further 15
min before being filtered. The filter bed was washed with a mixture of
water (136 mL) and toluene (136 mL). The organic layer was discarded.
Potassium carbonate (134.14 g, 0.98 mol) was added to the aqueous phase
followed by a solution of di-tert-butyl dicarbonate (116.5 g, 0.53 mol)
in 2-methyltetrahydrofuran (544 mL). The biphasic mixture was stirred at
40 °C for 2 h. Harborlite (12.0 g) was added and the reaction mixture was
stirred for a further 15 minutes. The mixture was filtered. The filter
bed was washed with a mixture of water (136 mL) and
2-methyltetrahydrofuran (136 mL). The aqueous layer was extracted with
2-methyltetrahydrofuran (272 mL). The organic layers were combined and
distilled at atmospheric pressure until the internal temperature reached
98 °C (~760 mL distillate collected). The residual solution was treated
with 5.55 M hydrochloric acid in isopropanol (238 mL, 1.32 mol). The
reaction mixture was heated to 40 °C for 18 h. The amine hydrochloride,
4, precipitated over this period. Heptane (204 mL) was added over 15 min
and the resulting suspension stirred at 20 °C for 16 h. The reaction
mixture was filtered and the isolated amine hydrochloride 4 washed with
2-methyltetrahydrofuran (102 mL) before being dried in the vacuum oven to
give the title compound. 68.2g @ 98.4% w/w, 77.1%. 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CD3SOCD3) δ: 9.02 (d, 2H), 4.55 (m, 1H), 1.58 (d, 3H). LCMS: 142 [M +
H]+. 1H NMR assay vs maleic acid internal standard 98.4% w/w.
Enantiomeric excess was determined by chiral HPLC (CrownPak CR+, aqueous
perchloric acid, &gt;99% ee).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM biotransformation, enzymic, stereoselective, optimization study, scalable
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Efficient Synthesis of (S)-1-(5-Fluoropyrimidin-2-yl)ethylamine Using an
ω-Transaminase Biocatalyst in a Two-Phase System
