$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of Ethyl
5-{[(4-Trifluoromethoxybenzyl)-amino]methyl}-furan-3-carboxylate
Hydrochloride (16). To a solution of ethyl 5-formylfuran-3-carboxylate
(15) (63.9 kg, 1.0 mol equiv) in toluene (208 L, 3.0 rel vol),
4-(trifluoromethoxy)benzylamine (79.9 kg, 1.1 mol equiv) was added,
stirring until the reaction was shown to be complete. Sodium borohydride
(18.0 kg, 1.25 mol equiv) was added and the resulting slurry cooled to
-5°C. Ethanol (480 L, 7.5 rel vol) was added, and the resulting solution
was quenched into aqueous hydrochloric acid (415 L, 6.5 mol equiv) to
crystallise. This slurry was heated to greater than 55°C and then cooled
to room temperature. Filtering and washing with aqueous ethanol and
drying at 40°C afforded the title compound 16. Ethyl
5-{[(4-Trifluoromethoxybenzyl)-amino]methyl}-furan-3-carboxylate
Hydrochloride (16) as a crystalline white solid, yield 75%. 1H NMR (400
MHz, d6-DMSO) δH 1.28 (3 H, t, 7.2 Hz), 4.24 (6 H, m), 6.97 (1 H, s),
7.44 (2 H, d, 7.9 Hz), 7.70 (2 H, d, 8.6 Hz), 8.46 (1 H, d, 1.0 Hz). 13C
NMR (400 MHz, DMSO) δ 162.0, 149.0, 148.6, 147.6, 132.4, 131.3, 121.0,
120.0, 119.8, 111.7, 60.3, 48.6, 41.8, 14.1. Mp = 158°C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM 64 kg scale (pilot plant)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Isoindolone formation via intramolecular Diels-Alder reaction
