$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM N6-(3,4-Difluorobenzyl)-N2-(2-dimethylaminoethyl)-4,N2-dimethylquinoline-2,6-diamine
(4v). Compound 4c (2.0 g, 7.8 mmol), 3,4-difluorobenzaldehyde (1.66 g,
11.7 mmol) and sodium methoxide (2.1 g, 38 mmol) were stirred in MeOH
(150 mL) at 40 °C. After 48 h NaBH4 (653 mg, 17 mmol) was added and the
mixture heated to 50 °C for a further 48 h. The reaction mixture was
allowed to cool before the volatiles were removed in vacuo. The residue
was taken up in 4 M HCl (50 mL) and washed with CH2Cl2 (30 mL). The
aqueous layer was then basified with 4 M NaOH to pH 10 and extracted with
CH2Cl2 (3 x 30 mL). The combined organic extracts was and washed with
brine (50 mL), dried (Na2SO4) and concentrated to yield the title
compound as a brown oil (1.69 g, 56%) which was used without further
purification.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
