$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (3S,4S,5R)-3-(4-Amino-3-fluoro-5-((1,1,1,3,3,3-hexafluoropropan-2-yl)oxy)benzyl)-5-(((4-(tert-butyl)pyridin-2-yl)methyl)amino)-4-hydroxytetrahydro-2H-thiopyran
1,1-dioxide (62c): To a solution of
(3R,4S,5S)-3-amino-5-(4-amino-3-fluoro-5-((1,1,1,3,3,3-hexafluoropropan-2-yl)oxy)benzyl)-4-hydroxytetrahydro-2H-thiopyran
1,1-dioxide (0.091 g, 0.2 mmol) in MeO-CH2Cl2 1:1 (2 mL) was added acetic
acid (0.012 g, 0.2 mmol), NaOAc (0.053 g, 0.64 mmol) and
4-tert-butyl-pyridine-2-carbaldehyde (0.041 g, 0.25 mmol) and the
reaction mixture was stirred for 17 h at 25 °C before NaBH3CN (0.021 g,
0.3 mmol) was added followed by stirring for 1 h. The reaction mixture
was acidified with 1N HCl, stirred for 15 min, basified with aqueous
ammonia and extracted with CH2Cl2/iPrOH. The combined organic layers were
washed with brine, dried over MgSO4, filtered and concentrated. The crude
product was purified by reverse-phase preparative HPLC to afford after
basification with aqueous ammonia and extraction with CH2Cl2, 0.066 g
(55%) of
(3S,4S,5R)-3-(4-amino-3-fluoro-5-((1,1,1,3,3,3-hexafluoropropan-2-yl)oxy)benzyl)-5-(((4-(tert-butyl)pyridin-2-yl)-methyl)amino)-4-hydroxytetrahydro-2H-thiopyran
1,1-dioxide as a colorless amorphous solid. 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ
8.40 (d, J = 4.8 Hz, 1H), 7.40 (s, 1H), 7.26 (m, 1H), 6.80 (s, 1H), 6.72
(d, J = 12.0 Hz, 1H), 6.39 (m, 1H), 5.45 (br s, 1H), 4.64 (s, 2H),
3.72-4.02 (m, 2H), 3.42 (m, 1H), 2.6-3.3 (m, 6H), 2.34 (dd, J = 13.3, 9.2
Hz, 1H), 2.01 (m, 1H), 1.27 (s, 9H); LC/MS (ESI, positive ion): m/z 602
(M+H); HRMS m/z 602.19148 [(M+H) + calcd for C25H31F7N3O4S + ,
602.19180].
