$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure A. tert-Butyl 3-(3-phenylureido)propylcarbamate (1
equiv) was added to a solution of 20% TFA and 80% CH2Cl2. After the
mixture was stirred for 3 h, the solvent was removed in vacuo. Residues
were re-dissolved in MeOH. Sodium methoxide (1 equiv) was added to the
mixture and stirred for 15 min. Appropriate aldehyde (1 equiv) and 10%
acetic acid were added to the mixture, and stirred for 0.5 h, followed by
NaCNBH3 (2 equiv). After the mixture was stirred overnight, the solvent
was removed in vacuo. The residues were purified by HPLC or silica gel
flash chromatography (1-10% (10% NH4OH, 90% MeOH), CH2Cl2). Colorless
Oil, yield 58%. Compound 4 ESI-MS, (M + H)+ (m/z): 348.9, 1H NMR (500
MHz, MeOD) δ 7.31 - 7.36 (m, 2H), 7.24 (t, J = 8.0 Hz, 2H), 6.93 - 7.00
(m, 2H), 6.88 (s, 1H), 6.84 (s, 1H), 3.77 (s, 3H), 3.72 (s, 2H), 3.26 (t,
J = 6.7 Hz, 2H), 2.66 (t, J = 7.1 Hz, 2H), 1.75 (p, J = 6.9 Hz, 2H).
