$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Compound 1. Intermediate 1b (1.65 g, 4.27 mmol) was dissolved in CH2Cl2
(5 mL/gram) and the same volume of 2N HCl/ether was added. The reaction
solution was allowed to stir for 2 hr at rt, after which time a white
precipitate formed. The solid was collected on a Buchner funnel and
rinsed with ether several times to afford the bis-HCl salt. A portion of
the salt (0.223 g, 0.623 mmol) was then dissolved in 1% AcOH/IPA (5.2 mL,
0.12 M), and 4-phenoxybenzaldehyde (0.123 g, 0.623 mmol) was added,
followed by sodium triacetoxyborohydride (0.349 g, 1.65 mmol). After
stirring for 2 hr, the reaction was quenched with 0.6 mL of sat. NaHCO3,
and the organics evaporated. The residue was taken up in CHCl3 and washed
with 1N NaOH (x2), dried, and filtered. Chromatography over 1-5% Et3N in
CH2Cl2 afforded the title compound (45.1 mg, 0.0961 mmol) in 15% yield.
Compound 1. , yield (45.1 mg, 0.0961 mmol, 15%) 1H NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d6)
δ ppm 1.67 - 1.87 (m, 4H), 2.48 - 2.67 (m, 4H, J = 6.27, 6.27 Hz), 2.90
(t, 2H, J = 7.29 Hz), 3.42 (s, 2H), 3.83 (s, 2H), 4.29 (t, 2H, J = 7.29
Hz), 6.41 (m, 1H), 6.85 (m, 2H), 6.90 - 6.98 (m, 2H), 6.98 - 7.09 (m,
2H), 7.17 - 7.28 (m, 3H), 7.38 (m, 2H), 7.47 (d, 1H, J = 8.14 Hz), 7.86
(m, 1H). MS (DCI/NH3) m/z 469.2 [M+H]+.
