$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 1.2. General procedures for the synthesis of
the compounds 5a−j To a stirred solution of 4 (2.81 g, 10.0 mmol) and
triethylamine (2.8 mL, 20.0 mmol) in 1, 2-dichloroethane (50 mL),
aldehyde (15.0 mmol) was added dropwise. The reaction mixture was
refluxed for 2 h and sodium tri-acetoxyborohydride (3.16 g,15.0 mmol) was
added into the reaction mixture slowly. The reaction solution was
refluxed till TLC analysis showed completion of the reaction. After
cooling down, the mixture was separated and washed successively with
water (20 mL), brine (20 mL). The organic layer was evaporated under
vacuum, and the residue was purified by flash chromatography over silica
gel or acidized with 3 N hydrochloride/ether (10 mL) to obtain the
desired product. 1.2.3. Methyl 12-N-3,4-dimethoxybenzylsophoridinate
dihydrochloride (5c) The title compound was prepared from 4 and
3,4-dimethoxybenzaldehyde in the same manner as described above. Yield:
59%; White solid. mp 78−80 °C; 1H NMR δ (ppm): 11.56 (s, 1H, NH), 10.57
(s, 1H, NH), 7.67-7.59 (m, 1H, Ph), 7.40-7.21 (m, 2H, Ph), 4.29-4.07 (m,
2H, 1"-H), 3.84 (s, 3H, OCH3), 3.79 (s, 3H, OCH3), 3.59 (s, 3H, OCH3),
3.22-3.11 (m, 5H, 2-H, 10-H, 11-H), 3.12-2.95 (m, 2H, 13-H), 2.95-2.72
(m, 2H, 3'-H), 2.30-1.86 (m, 5H, 5-H, 6-H, 7-H, 1'-H), 1.74-1.53 (m, 4H,
9-H, 2'-H), 1.52-1.21 (m, 4H, 3-H, 8-H), 1.11-0.87 (m, 2H, 4-H); 13C NMR
δ (ppm): 171.7, 152.4, 147.3, 124.4, 122.8, 122.5, 114.1, 61.3, 61.2,
60.2, 55.9, 55.1, 51.7, 51.5, 49.9, 48.5, 44.1, 33.3, 31.6, 25.6, 24.7,
22.2, 21.8, 21.2, 17.1; HRMS: calcd for C25H38N2O4.2HCl [M−2HCl+H]+,
431.2904; found, 431.2913.
