$DATUM (2S)-2-[[(3β,15α,16α,23R,24S)-24-Acetyloxy-16,23-epoxy-25-hydroxy-9,19-cyclolanostan-15-one-3-yl]oxy]-4-[1-(tertbutoxycarbonyl)azetidin-3-yl]morpholine
(3). A solution of 1-Boc-3-(amino)azetidine (13.64 g, 79.2 mmol) in MeOH
(250 mL) was treated with 1 M HCl(aq) (79.2 mL, 79.2 mmol), and the
mixture was stirred for 10 min and then concentrated under reduced
pressure to provide the amine hydrochloride salt as a white powder. To
the amine salt was added a solution of crude dialdehyde 2a in 9:1
EtOH/AcOH (500 mL) followed by NaBH(OAc)3 (48.10 g, 226.3 mmol). The
reaction mixture was stirred at RT for 90 min and then transferred to a
mixture of CH2Cl2 (1 L) and H2O (1 L), and the layers were separated. The
aqueous layer was extracted with CH2Cl2 (2 x 500 mL), and then the
combined organic layers were dried (Na2SO4), filtered, and concentrated
under reduced pressure to provide morpholine 3. To the crude product was
added toluene, which was removed under reduced pressure to azeotrope off
any residual AcOH. This process was repeated, and then the crude material
was carried on without further purification. Quantitative yield. MS
(ESI+): m/z = 771 [M + H]+.
