$DATUM Step F. A mixture of
6-amino-4-methyl-2,10-dihydro-9-oxa-1,2,4a-triaza-phenanthren-3-one
(0.232 g, 1.00 mmol) and tert-butyl 3-oxoazetidine-1-carboxylate (1.71 g,
10.0 mmol) in MeOH (20 mL) and AcOH (2 mL) was heated at reflux for 1.5
h. The reaction mixture was cooled to ambient temperature and sodium
cyanoborohydride (0.251 g, 4.0 mmol) was added. The reaction mixture was
heated at reflux for 2 h then cooled to ambient temperature and
concentrated in vacuo. The residue was purified by column chromatography
on silica gel (eluting with 60% to 75% EtOAc in petroleum ether).
3-(4-methyl-3-oxo-2,3,4,10-tetrahydro-9-oxa-1,2,4a-triaza-phenanthren-6-ylamino)-azetidine-1-carboxylic
acid tert-butyl ester (Compound 15x, 0.313 g, 81%) as a yellow oil. 1H
NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz): δ 8.55 (s, 1H), 6.86 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H), 6.14 (s,
2H), 4.69 (q, J = 6.7 Hz, 1H), 4.54 (q, J = 10.4 Hz, 2H), 4.30 (m, 2H),
4.16 (m, 1H), 4.08 (m, 1H), 3.74 (m, 2H), 1.51 (d, J = 6.8 Hz, 3H),1.47
(s, 9H). LC/MS (Table 1, Method 2) Rt = 1.015 min; MS m/z: 388.2 [M+1]+.
