$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Step D. A solution of
2-(6-amino-3-thioxo-2,3-dihydro-benzo[1,4]oxazin-4-yl)-butyric acid ethyl
ester (0.546 g, 1.855 mmol) and tert-butyl 3-oxoazetidine-1-carboxylate
(0.381 g, 2.226 mmol) in MeOH (20 mL) and AcOH (2 mL) was stirred at
ambient temperature for 1 h. Sodium cyanoborohydride (0.175 g, 2.78 mmol)
was added and the reaction mixture was stirred at ambient temperature
overnight. The reaction mixture was concentrated in vacuo and the residue
was purified by chromatography on silica gel (eluting with 5% to 25%
EtOAc in petroleum ether). Step D. tert-Butyl
3-oxoazetidine-1-carboxylate (2.4 equiv) and sodium cyanoborohydride (7.6
vol equiv) in MeOH (10 vol equiv) and AcOH (1 vol equiv) at room
temperature overnight; 0.27 g, 58%, as an oil.
