$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Step A. To a solution of
6-amino-2,10-dihydro-9-oxa-1,2,4a-triazaphenanthren-3-one (intermediate
obtained at Step D during preparation of compound 15a, 0.060 g, 0.275
mmol) in MeOH (3 mL) and AcOH (0.3 mL) was added
4-oxo-azepane-1-carboxylic acid tert-butyl ester (0.117 g, 0.55 mmol) and
the reaction mixture was stirred at ambient temperature for 1 h. NaBH3CN
(0.052 g, 0.825 mmol) was added and the reaction mixture was stirred at
ambient temperature for 16 h. The reaction mixture was concentrated in
vacuo and the residue was purified by preparative-HPLC (Column: Gemini
150x25 mm, 5 μm, Mobile phase: A: H2O (0.05% HCl) B: acetonitrile,
Gradient: B from 15% to 40% in 15 min, Flow rate: 30 mL/min, Wavelength:
220 nm). Prepared according to the procedure of 15g using: Step A:
3-formylazetidine-1-carboxylic acid tert-butyl ester (1.2 equiv), MeOH
(14 vol equiv), AcOH (0.7 vol equiv) and NaBH3CN (1.5 equiv) at ambient
temperature overnight; 0.04 g, 36%, as a yellow solid.
