$DATUM Methyl
4-({6-[(tert-Butoxycarbonyl)amino]hexyl}amino)-5-chloro-2-methoxybenzoate
(5). Ester 3 (0.9 g, 3.94 mmol), aldehyde 4 27 (1.8 g, 7.78 mmol), and
glacial acetic acid (1.43 mL) were mixed in 1,2-dichloroethane (30 mL).
Then, sodium triacetoxyborohydride (2.65 g, 12.5 mmol) was added to the
above solution, and the reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature
under argon atmosphere for 24 h. After concentration, the product was
taken up with AcOEt (30 mL), washed with saturated aqueous NaHCO3 (3 × 30
mL) and with saturated aqueous NaCl (30 mL). The AcOEt layer was dried
(MgSO4) and concentrated. The crude product was chromatographed on silica
gel (petroleum ether/AcOEt 70:30) to give 1.38 g (79%) of 5 as a
colorless oil. Rf (petroleum ether/AcOEt 70:30) 0.44; 1H NMR (200 MHz): δ
7.8 (s, 1H), 6.12 (s, 1H), 4.66 (bs, 1H), 4.5 (bs, 1H), 3.9 (s, 3H), 3.8
(s, 3H), 3.15 (m, 4H), 1.7 (m, 2H), 1.43 (m, 15H). Anal. (C20H31ClN2O5)
C, H, N.
