$DATUM Synthesis of compound 28:
7-bromo-1,2,3,4-tetrahydronaphthalene-1-carbaldehyde (27) (0.267 g, 1.12
mmol) was dissolved in dry 1,2-dichloroethane (20 mL, 0.2 mol) then
2-aminobenzothiazole (0.217 g, 1.44 mmol) was added followed by sodium
triacetoxyborohydride (0.413 g, 1.95 mmol). The mixture was stirred
overnight. The mixture was then diluted with saturated aqueous sodium
bicarbonate, extracted three times with 10% methanol in dichloromethane,
dried over anhydrous magnesium sulfate, filtered, and concentrated. The
mixture was chromatographed through silica gel (4g, 0-30% ethyl acetate
in hexanes).
N-((7-bromo-1,2,3,4-tetrahydronaphthalen-1-yl)methyl)benzo[d]thiazol-2-amine
(28). Yield: (0.194g, 0.520mmol, 46%).
